{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat Makefile; sed -n '1,260p' formal/run_all.sh; rg -n 'div|ten|10|completion|latency' cores/bench/test/test_*.py; rg --files cores/bench/test tools/eval fpga | head -100\"", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[24320 of 27392 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a4d3a392eb98c940]…\nnstraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\nfpga/constraints/clock.sdc\nfpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\nfpga/core_bench.sv\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl\nfpga/scripts/nextpnr_run.sh\ntools/eval/holdout.py\ntools/eval/gowin.py\ntools/eval/formal.py\ntools/eval/test_gate_sanity.py\ntools/eval/_subprocess.py\ntools/eval/test_holdout.py\ntools/eval/fpga.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_workdir_cleanup.py\ntools/eval/test_rvfi_lint.py\ntools/eval/test_process_reaper.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_reclassify.py\ntools/eval/rvfi_lint.py\ntools/eval/test_remove_path.py\ntools/eval/test_subprocess_pgroup.py\ntools/eval/__init__.py\ntools/eval/test_slots.py\ntools/eval/test_bench_stall_gen.py\ntools/eval/test_fpga_report.py\ntools/eval/test_formal_nret.py\ntools/eval/cosim.py\ntools/eval/_slots.py\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_core_div.py\ncores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
