{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short --untracked-files=all; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n# Implementation notes\n\nImplemented four unrolled radix-4 digits per LOOP clock in rtl/div_unit.sv.\nPREP normalizes the divisor to its unsigned magnitude and registers 34-bit\nB and 3B; 2B is a wiring shift of registered B. Every digit computes three\nparallel 35-bit subtractions of the full 34-bit partial dividend and divisor\nmultiples. The inverse borrow bits select the quotient digit and drive the\nspecified flat one-hot AND/OR remainder mux. Only the selected remainder\nis retained as 32 bits.\n\nThe state machine, four LOOP clocks, six-clock completion after capture,\nstart/busy/done/accept behavior, magnitude preparation, sign correction,\ndivide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 overrides, reset behavior, and ALTOPS formulas\nare preserved. No other RTL modules, frontend control, RVFI logic, core.yaml,\nor retirement width were changed; nret remains 1. There are no architectural\ndeviations from the hypothesis.\n\nExpanded test/test_div_unit.py with B/2B/3B boundaries and neighboring values,\nhigh unsigned divisors, both upper carries of 3B, every quotient digit in\neach LOOP iteration, every signed operand sign combination, and deterministic\nrandom operands biased toward long quotients. Retained existing arithmetic,\nzero-divisor, signed-overflow, exact six-clock latency, and reset-cancellation\nchecks. Added result stability before completion, ignored early accepts,\nchanging requests while DONE is held, and simultaneous start/accept behavior.\nThe existing core tests and ten-clock adjacent-retirement bounds are unchanged.\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- Strict Verilator -Wall lint: PASS, both real arithmetic and ALTOPS builds.\n- pytest -q cores/bench/test/: PASS, 9 runner cases (both real and ALTOPS\n  divider/core variants), 46.07 seconds.\n- NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench: PASS, selftest RVFI comparison with and\n  without stalls, plus stalled CoreMark canonical CRCs and validation text.\n- Stalled CoreMark: bracketed cycles 4,491,485 (start 15,801, stop 4,507,286),\n  10 iterations, no out-of-bounds access, all canonical CRCs correct.\n- RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh:\n  PASS on the first attempt, 53 passed, 0 failed. No counterexamples or\n  formal fix attempts.\n- make timing TARGET=bench: PASS, placement option 0 Fmax 38.682 MHz,\n  33 logic levels, 3,453 logic cells, 745 registers. Worst path is\n  quotient_q[30] to remainder_q[7] inside the divider: 31.146 ns arrival,\n  136 path cells (champion: 38.355 ns, 252 cells, 48 levels).\n- Gowin placement options 0/1/2: 38.682 / 39.675 / 39.675 MHz; all PASS.\n  Median Fmax 39.675 MHz, 29.59% above champion 30.617 MHz, exceeding the\n  4.6% threshold. Calculated fitness from this median and measured CoreMark\n  bracket is approximately 88.33 iterations/second (champion 68.17).\n\nConcern: parallel trial subtractors increase logic area and divisor fanout.\nOption 0 uses 443 more logic cells and 33 more registers than the champion;\nits critical path remains within LOOP, so PREP magnitude-plus-3B did not\nbecome the limiting path in that placement. Real arithmetic has been tested\nwith cocotb and cosim; the required fast formal suite uses ALTOPS and is not\na proof of unrestricted real division arithmetic.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
