{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_30", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\n# Implementation notes\n\nImplemented the hypothesis in `rtl/reg_file.sv`: the 32x32 data array has\nGowin's `syn_ramstyle=\"distributed_ram\"` attribute and no reset assignment.\nIts only update is a nonblocking synchronous nonzero write with reset low.\nA synchronously reset 32-bit `written_q` bitmap masks unwritten values on\nboth asynchronous read ports. Read priority remains x0, current write\nbypass, written storage, then zero. The bypass remains active during reset;\nreset/write collisions clear validity and do not write the data array.\n\nOnly the register-file RTL changed. The interface, pipeline controls,\nlatencies, WB refresh, EX forwarding, M/ALTOPS lifecycle, memory requests,\npredictor and single-channel RVFI contract remain unchanged. No deviation\nfrom the proposed hardware change.\n\nRetained every original register-file test and added an independent model\ncontaining architectural register values only. Added both-port checks\nbefore and after each edge and after removing bypass, exhaustive 32x32\nread-address pairs, all writable addresses, zero-valued writes, x0 writes,\ndirty repeated resets, held resets, reset/write collisions at every\nwritable address, first writes after reset, and 2,000 deterministic random\ncycles (seed 0x52465345). Original pipeline, core M, decoder and predictor\ntests remain unchanged.\n\nLocal validation:\n- Required Verilator lint: PASS, no warnings.\n- Register-file tests: PASS, all five original and both new tests.\n- Original unit suite: PASS. Together with the register-file tests, 12\n  pytest runners and 129 cocotb cases passed, including real and ALTOPS\n  divider, M-unit and core-M tests.\n- Full `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash\n  formal/run_all.sh` suite with nret=1/ALTOPS: **PASS on the first attempt,\n  53 passed, 0 failed**, including liveness and register consistency.\n  No counterexamples or RTL fix attempts. Local run log:\n  `formal/last_run-wp6HWFYCT.log`.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: PASS. Re-ran the unchanged cosim gate\n  after building all three committed random programs: five ELFs passed\n  (selftest, random1/2/3 and CoreMark). Each small program passed full RVFI\n  trace comparison with both buses ready and with independent random\n  imem+dmem stalls. Also checked imem-only and dmem-only stalls for all\n  four small programs: all eight additional comparisons passed.\n- CoreMark: PASS canonical CRC/UART validation, EBREAK completion and\n  bounds checks. `run_coremark_ipc` reports exactly 4,378,154 bracketed\n  marker cycles for 10 iterations, identical to the champion.\n- Gowin: all three scored placement options completed successfully.\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Worst arrival (ns) |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 0 | 67.925 | 20.016 |\n| 1 | 64.826 | 20.720 |\n| 2 | 64.826 | 20.720 |\n\nThe scored median is **64.826 MHz** and calculated fitness is\n**148.07 iterations/second** at the unchanged marker count. The median\ngain is 0.989% over 64.191 MHz. This candidate does **not** clear the\n67.144 MHz / 153.365 iterations/second acceptance thresholds; the strong\noption-0 prototype result reproduced but did not hold across placements.\n\nAll placements report 4,336 logic cells, 1,135 registers, 32 LUT RAMs,\nfour BSRAMs and two DSPs. The synthesis resource XML specifically reports\n`u_rf` with `Ssram=\"32\"` and `Register=\"31\"`, and the synthesis log\nextracts RAM for `regs`, confirming the data array actually maps to LUT\nRAM. Reports are under `cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p{0,1,2}`.\n\nTiming is limited by WB register-tag control through ID/EX and into fetch\ncontrol; divider paths are also close to the worst path. Actual LUT-RAM\nmapping and architectural marker-cycle preservation are verified. The\nhardware remains the exact proposed micro-optimization; no pipeline or\nunrelated changes were added to chase the missing acceptance margin.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
