{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"The added tests exposed two testbench assumptions: random stalls can delay branch decode and leave three queued tokens at recovery, and a data hold postpones the load-use bubble. I’ve corrected those checks while retaining exact FIFO and architectural checks. Timing is still below the required margin, so I’m simplifying the slot-update enables within the specified topology.\n"}}
