{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'pytest|cocotb|div_unit|CORE_TARGET|COREMARK|fpga|timing|cosim' cores/bench/test test tools/eval formal/checks_si.cfg CLAUDE.md\"", "aggregated_output": "CLAUDE.md:11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\nCLAUDE.md:16:| 5b | M-extension arithmetic produces RV32M-correct bit results                                                | cocotb `test_alu.py` + `make formal-deep`    |\nCLAUDE.md:18:| 7 | CoreMark CRCs match the canonical 2K-config perf run (`TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000`, `-O3`, `ITERATIONS=10`): `seedcrc=0xe9f5`, `crclist=0xe714`, `crcmatrix=0x1fd7`, `crcstate=0x8e3a`, `crcfinal=0xfcaf` | `validate_coremark_uart` in fpga eval (`COREMARK_EXPECTED` in `tools/eval/fpga.py` is the source of truth) |\nCLAUDE.md:19:| 8 | CoreMark timing brackets `start_time` / `stop_time` markers — total elapsed cycles do NOT count            | MMIO writes at `0x10000100` / `0x10000104`   |\nCLAUDE.md:39:- `fpga/core_bench.sv`, `fpga/core_bench_si.sv`, `fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv`, `fpga/scripts/*`,\nCLAUDE.md:40:  `fpga/constraints/*` — they define the FPGA fitness contract\nCLAUDE.md:42:- `test/cosim/main.cpp`, `test/cosim/reference.py`, `test/cosim/run_cosim.py`\nCLAUDE.md:43:  — Verilator harness + Python ISS = the cosim contract.\nCLAUDE.md:57:Everything under `cores/<TARGET>/rtl/` and the cocotb unit tests under