{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_31", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; git diff --numstat; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/m_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_core_div.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n143\t65\tcores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n1\t1\tcores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n1\t1\tcores/bench/rtl/m_unit.sv\n29\t0\tcores/bench/test/test_core_div.py\n77\t0\tcores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n# Divider launch isolation implementation\n\nImplemented the proposed divider topology in `rtl/div_unit.sv`: preserved raw\n`a`, `b`, and `op` launch registers; one PREP edge; and six identical five-bit\nupdates, each consisting of a parallel radix-8 trial/select followed by a\nparallel radix-4 trial/select. Both trial groups use 35-bit operands and\n36-bit subtract results, borrow-based fits, mutually exclusive digit terms,\nand balanced masked-residual OR trees. PREP uses the explicit sixteen-entry\ntwo-bit seed table and full-width D through 7D multiples, each non-power-of-two\nmultiple computed with one addition/subtraction from wired shifts.\n\nSign, zero-divisor and overflow correction remains combinational from frozen\nDONE state to acceptance. The original dividend and operation remain in the\npreserved launch registers throughout PREP, LOOP, and held DONE. ALTOPS retains\nthe exact four formulas and follows the same raw-launch/PREP/six-LOOP lifecycle.\nThere is no additional completion edge. The pipeline, predictor, multiplier,\ntop-level IO, retirement path, and formal contract are unchanged; only divider\nlifecycle comments changed in `ex_stage.sv` and `m_unit.sv`.\n\nRetained every existing divider and core dependency test. Added exhaustive\ntwo-bit seed pairs, PREP state and exact seed checks, frozen raw operand checks,\nall radix digit threshold boundaries at every digit position, high-divisor\nrandom operands, quotient/remainder identities and sign bounds, and mixed M\ndependencies with older memory stalls. Existing reset, held completion,\nadjacent nine-clock retirement and ten-clock transfer-to-DIV checks remain.\n\nCompleted local validation:\n\n- Verilator lint: PASS, without warnings, in\n…[1237 of 4309 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4298d79ea98c19aa]…\n0 iterations/second, 8.11% above 124.78 and above\n  the 4.6% acceptance threshold (57.143 MHz at unchanged marker cycles).\n- Gowin's timing report contains actual `raw_a_q`, `raw_b_q` and `raw_op_q`\n  register endpoints, confirming the launch boundary survives vendor synthesis.\n\nThe plain cosim Makefile invocation initially defaulted the C++ harness to\nNRET=2 and failed to build this declared NRET=1 core. Supplying NRET=1 corrected\nthe local invocation; no harness, Makefile, core.yaml, or wrapper was edited.\n\nNo architectural deviation from the hypothesis. Fresh timing is lower than\nthe proposal's scratch evidence (59.061 versus 61.075 MHz median), but exceeds\nthe stated acceptance bar with unchanged cycles. These numbers come from the\nfresh unmodified evaluator, not the proposal's prototype measurements.\nFull real-arithmetic SMT (`formal-deep`) has not been run; exact arithmetic is\nchecked locally by cocotb and cosim, while the unchanged full formal suite uses\nALTOPS as specified by the evaluation contract.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
