or 3 and the corresponding new remainder.\\nDerive trial validity from each widened subtraction's borrow bit rather\\nthan instantiating a separate magnitude comparator followed by another\\nsubtraction. Use sufficient unsigned width throughout: divisor\\nmultiples and partial dividends require 34 bits, and trial differences\\nrequire 35 bits to retain underflow\n…[2732 of 5804 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c8b3b57aba4b5862]…\n with\\nbit 31 set, powers of two, values around radix-4 digit boundaries,\\nand consecutive switches between signed and unsigned operations.\\nRequire the existing formal and stalled CoreMark cosim gates to pass,\\nthen compare Gowin Fmax and fitness against the 4.6 percent threshold.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 13.98, \"delta_pct\": 15.35, \"vs_baseline\": 15.35, \"fmax_mhz\": 6.277, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6045, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [6.179, 6.277, 6.277], \"perturbations\": [[0, 6.179, 143], [1, 6.277, 144], [2, 6.277, 144]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -156.85, \"arrival_ns\": 167.145, \"logic_cells\": 452, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 143, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T01:31:46.776842Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
