{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Split normal and recovery fetch-address registers\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 146.62 at median Fmax 64.191 MHz and 4378154\\nCoreMark marker cycles. Its reported worst Gowin path now ends at\\nu_if/pc after register-file, ID and EX logic: 21.444 ns and 37 cells.\\nPredictor accuracy is already high: prior profiling found only 41558\\nconditional direction errors and 13735 JALRs in the timed trace.\\nEliminating all of them would save only about 1.3 percent of cycles.\\nLarger tables, carried direct successors, LUT-RAM initialization and\\nbanked counter feedback have not produced an accepted gain. The new\\nopportunity is to remove recovery arbitration from the target's\\nregister input now that EX-to-fetch feedback limits timing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion scores 146.62 at median Fmax 64.191 MHz and 4378154\\nCoreMark marker cycles. Its reported worst Gowin path now ends at\\nu_if/pc after register-file, ID and EX logic: 21.444 ns and 37 cells.\\nPredictor accuracy is already high: prior profiling found only 41558\\nconditional direction errors and 13735 JALRs in the timed trace.\\nEliminating all of them would save only about 1.3 percent of cycles.\\nLarger tables, carried direct successors, LUT-RAM initialization and\\nbanked counter feedback have not produced an accepted gain. The new\\nopportunity is to remove recovery arbitration from the target's\\nregister input now that EX-to-fetch feedback limits timing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the fetch address into a normal-PC register and an independently\\ncaptured recovery-target register, selected AFTER their clocked\\nboundaries by a registered recovery bit. Preserve the current BHT,\\ndirect JAL prediction and one-bit EX mismatch detection. This is one\\npredictor recovery-topology change, with identical accepted fetches\\nand no additional recovery cycle or pipeline stage.\\n\\nIn IF, capture the existing full-width EX redirect_target into a\\ndedicated register on every non-reset edge, unco\n…[83365 of 86437 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9bee62172dcb9e7f]…\n\"delta_pct\": 4.63, \"vs_baseline\": 1407.67, \"fmax_mhz\": 80.002, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4378154, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6386, \"ff\": 2170, \"seeds\": [73.007, 80.002, 80.002], \"perturbations\": [[0, 73.007, 14], [1, 80.002, 15], [2, 80.002, 15]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_5_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_5_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -8.697, \"arrival_ns\": 18.992, \"logic_cells\": 37, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T07:21:49.588470Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r10s0 (improvement, +4.63%): Using monotonic trial-fit flags directly in balanced radix-8/radix-4 residual mux trees bypasses adjacent-fit one-hot decoding between divider carry chains, improving median Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles while preserving native trial arithmetic and quotient encoding.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
