{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r10s0',\n 'title':'Balanced threshold muxes for divider residual selection',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.65 at 76.466 MHz with 4378154 CoreMark marker\ncycles. Recent micro_opt forwarding/comparator candidates repeatedly\nexpose a roughly 19 ns quotient/remainder-to-remainder path inside\nu_ex/u_m/u_div. Its six LOOP clocks each contain a radix-8 digit followed\nby a radix-4 digit. Each round currently converts ordered trial-borrow\nflags into adjacent-fit one-hot enables before selecting residual data.\nOptimize that repeated selection rather than changing pipeline depth\nor the successful native FPGA carry arithmetic. Earlier micro_opt\nhistory and LESSONS.md were reviewed; no recorded attempt uses a\nbalanced threshold decision tree at these two residual selections.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace only the two divider residual masked-OR networks with balanced\nbinary threshold mux trees, using existing fit flags directly. Preserve\nall native 36-bit trial subtractions and all registered arithmetic.\nThis is one combinational selection micro-optimization inside div_unit.\n\nThe seven radix-8 trials use ordered multiples D,2D,...,7D. Their fit\nflags are monotonic: if kD fits, every smaller multiple also fits. Use\nfit8[4] to choose the upper or lower half of the eight residuals,\nfit8[6]/fit8[2] to choose a pair in that half, and fit8[7]/fit8[5]/\nfit8[3]/fit8[1] for the final pair decision. Implement exactly:\n  residual8 = fit8[4]\n    ? (fit8[6] ? (fit8[7] ? trial8[7][34:0] : trial8[6][34:0])\n               : (fit8[5] ? trial8[5][34:0] : trial8[4][34:0]))\n    : (fit8[2] ? (fit8[3] ? trial8[3][34:0] : trial8[2][34:0])\n               : (fit8[1] ? trial8[1][34:0] : numerator8));\nFor radix-4 use the analogous two-level selection:\n  residual4 = fit4[2]\n    ? (fit4[3] ? trial4[3][34:0] : trial4[2][34:0])\n    : (fit4[1] ? trial4[1][34:0] : numerator4);\nKeep the existing quotient digit encoding and select8/select4 decoding\nfor digit generation. Do not substitute a serial priority chain or\nchange digit encoding without fresh timing evidence.\n\nThis selects the largest fitting multiple exactly as the original\none-hot network, including D=0 (all fits true, selecting digit 7/3).\nThe maximum multiple 7D fits in 35 bits; native trials still use 36\nbits including borrow. Keep every upper multiple bit, radix-4's\nleading numerator zero, residual truncation and all exact arithmetic.\nBoth muxes use the same existing fit and trial signals. Bypassing\nadjacent-fit enable decoding should reduce serial selection depth and\nfanout between the two carry-chain rounds while reducing logic area.\n\nPreserve raw operand capture, the exact two-bit PREP seed and divisor\nmultiples, six five-bit LOOP edges, all state transitions, division\nlaunch/completion/accept timing, sign correction, zero-divisor and\nINT_MIN/-1 handling, stable DONE outputs and reset. Preserve every\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formula and completion clock. Leave M integration,\nheld operands, independent execution during older memory stalls,\nfrontend, predictor, memory requests, nret=1 public IO and all RVFI\nsemantics and invariants unchanged. No new helper module or register.\n\nAn isolated prototype with exactly these two residual mux replacements\nand otherwise unchanged champion RTL measured 73.007/80.002/80.002 MHz\nfor Gowin placement options 0/1/2: median 80.002 MHz, a 4.624 percent\nfrequency increase. Option-0 area was 6386 logic cells and 2170 registers,\nwith unchanged 0 LUT-RAM, 4 BSRAM and 2 DSP. Its worst reported path\nmoved to WB-to-fetch feedback. This is a real circuit change; the gain\nis only just above the 4.6 percent acceptance margin and remains\nsensitive to other nearly critical paths. It is a prototype timing\nresult, not an evaluator acceptance or completed formal proof.\n\nAt unchanged marker cycles, acceptance needs median Fmax above\n79.983436 MHz and fitness above 182.6839. Expect about 5 percent with\nmedium confidence, and score all three vendor placement options.\nRequire exact combinational equivalence on every reachable monotonic\nfit pattern and widened trial operand pair, existing real/ALTOPS\ndivider/M/core tests with unchanged latency and progress bounds,\nunchanged formal gates, ready and stalled ISS cosim, canonical CoreMark\nCRC/UART/bounds/MMIO marker validation and exactly 4378154 measured\nCoreMark cycles. Do not count an unvalidated timing result as fitness.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Replace only residual8 and residual4 masked one-hot OR selection with\nthe specified balanced fit-threshold mux trees. Retain native trial\nsubtraction, fit polarity, one-hot quotient digit encoding, full\nwidths, seed/multiples, all register edges, state and handshake timing,\nsign/exception correction, reset and ALTOPS behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Retain all current tests and exact completion/held-result assertions.\nAdd directed cases covering each radix-8 and radix-4 threshold at\nkD-1/kD/kD+1, high unsigned divisors and full-width multiple carries.\nCheck monotonic fit flags and selected residuals against an independent\nlargest-fitting-multiple reference through all six LOOP edges, with\nzero divisors, all signed combinations, overflow, reset and DONE holds.\nRequire arithmetic and core progress/stall checks in real and ALTOPS\nmodes; preserve all formal and canonical stalled CoreMark gates.\n'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis written and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
