ned division and remainder expressions in alu.sv are the\\nstrongest candidate for this deep arithmetic path. CoreMark fitness\\nscales directly with Fmax when instruction latency and cycle count stay\\nconstant. There are no earlier bench hypotheses or recorded lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one shared, fully\\ncombinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divider. Convert operands to\\nunsigned magn\n…[106845 of 109917 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2076fb688855db5c]…\n\"delta_pct\": 4.63, \"vs_baseline\": 1407.67, \"fmax_mhz\": 80.002, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4378154, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6386, \"ff\": 2170, \"seeds\": [73.007, 80.002, 80.002], \"perturbations\": [[0, 73.007, 14], [1, 80.002, 15], [2, 80.002, 15]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_5_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_5_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -8.697, \"arrival_ns\": 18.992, \"logic_cells\": 37, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T07:21:49.588470Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r10s0 (improvement, +4.63%): Using monotonic trial-fit flags directly in balanced radix-8/radix-4 residual mux trees bypasses adjacent-fit one-hot decoding between divider carry chains, improving median Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles while preserving native trial arithmetic and quotient encoding.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
