its.\n  Do not introduce a new late branch-op mux or prediction XOR in the\n  recovery path. Keep all decode predicates and their capture intact.\n\n  This is one local comparator topology micro-optimization. The four\n  short native comparisons run concurrently, followed by two balan\n…[1541 of 4613 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ced6798b863fd290]…\nim and canonical CoreMark\n  CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation. At unchanged cycles acceptance\n  requires median Fmax above 83.6821 MHz and fitness above 191.13558.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Build unsigned equality and less-than from four concurrent byte\n      comparisons and a balanced pair/pair combination. Derive signed\n      less-than by sign correction, and reuse the three relation bits\n      in existing architectural branch cases and recovery predicates.\n      Retain every surrounding control equation, stage and arithmetic.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all current assertions. Add architectural branch vectors\n      for each byte-order boundary and all six relations, including\n      sign changes and contradictory lower slices, across forwarded\n      writers, load dependencies, prolonged data holds, prediction\n      recovery and independent stalls. Keep progress and trap checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
