{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r12s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-001-r12s0\ntitle: \"Segmented carry-select arithmetic in the integer ALU\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 182.73 at 80.002 MHz with 4378154 CoreMark marker\n  cycles. The latest two alternative implementations expose a WB-to-EX\n  path ending at alu_result bits 28 or 30 through u_alu. Prior comparator,\n  forwarding-selector and predictor rewrites did not clear the acceptance\n  margin. Target the integer arithmetic carry path at its existing\n  register boundaries rather than adding instruction latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the native full-width ADD and SUB result expressions in alu.sv\n  with explicitly segmented combinational carry-select arithmetic. Divide\n  the 32-bit result into four eight-bit blocks. Compute each upper block's\n  sum for carry-in zero and one concurrently, and select the correct sum\n  using a balanced block carry network. Compute block propagate from all\n  eight bit-propagates and block generate from the carry-out of the local\n  carry-zero addition. Derive carries at bit 8, 16 and 24 with expanded\n  group generate/propagate expressions, avoiding a serial chain of three\n  carry-select muxes. For SUB use a + ~b + 1 with explicit unsigned widths;\n  all results are modulo 2^32. Retain native operators inside the short\n  blocks so Gowin can use its local carry resources. The new helper is\n  purely combinational and must work for arbitrary inputs and carry-in.\n\n  This is one local arithmetic topology optimization. Keep SLT/SLTU,\n  shifts, Boolean results, ALU operation encodings and default-zero behavior\n  unchanged. Preserve EX operand forwarding and result arbitration,\n  dedicated memory request arithmetic, branch recovery and predictor\n  training, multiplier/divider hardware and ALTOPS behavior, all pipeline\n  acceptance and retirement cycles, nret=1 and the public IO contract.\n  Change no correctness assertion or formal progress bound.\n\n  Prove complete ALU equivalence for every operation and operand pair and\n  require the existing formal, unit and ready/stalled ISS cosim gates.\n  CoreMark must retain the canonical CRCs, UART, bounds and marker checks\n  with exactly 4378154 measured cycles. At unchanged throughput a median\n  Gowin Fmax above 83.683 MHz is needed to clear the 4.6 percent margin.\n  Expected gain is eight percent, unmeasured; duplicated upper-block\n  arithmetic, routing and the unchanged divider/branch paths can cap or\n  reverse the gain. Inspect vendor timing and all scored placements.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Route only ALU_ADD and ALU_SUB through explicit four-block unsigned\n      carry-select arithmetic with a balanced group-carry network. Keep\n      every other operation, combinational interface and operation value\n      identical. Keep short block additions expressed with native plus.\n  - file: rtl/fast_add32.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a combinational 32-bit segmented adder with explicit nine-bit\n      local trials, eight-bit propagate reductions, expanded block carry\n      equations and selection of upper sums. Expose a, b, carry-in and\n      the modulo-2^32 sum; use no FPGA-specific primitives or registers.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all existing checks. Add independent integer-reference ADD\n      and SUB vectors covering carries and borrows across bits 8, 16 and\n      24, all-propagate chains, zero, signed extrema and deterministic\n      random operands. Require unchanged full combinational equivalence\n      and existing pipeline/cosim/formal correctness gates.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
