{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d.get('outcome'),d.get('delta_pct'),d.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  print('path',d.get('critical_path'))\n  print('notes',d.get('implementation_notes'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print('hypothesis',h.get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-4a6c0e6 Baseline retest for cores/bench improvement 0.0 5.442\npath {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nnotes \nhypothesis \nhyp-20261001-001-r1s0 Shared radix-4 combinational divider with borrow-based digit selection regression 15.35 6.277\npath {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -156.85, 'arrival_ns': 167.145, 'logic_cells': 452, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nnotes \nhypothesis Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one shared, fully\ncombinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divider. Convert operands to\nunsigned magnitudes for DIV and REM, and use the original bit patterns\nfor DIVU and REMU. Precompute widened divisor multiples B, 2B and 3B.\nUnroll 16 digit stages, consuming the dividend from its most significant\npair of bits to its least significant pair. At each stage form the\nwidened partial dividend P = 4*remainder + next_pair, calculate P-B,\nP-2B and P-3B in parallel, and select the largest nonnegative trial to\nemit quotient digit 0, 1, 2 or 3 and the corresponding new remainder.\nDerive trial validity from each widened subtraction's borrow bit rather\nthan instantiating a separate magnitude comparator followed by another\nsubtraction. Use sufficient unsigned width throughout: divisor\nmultiples and partial dividends require 34 bits, and trial differences\nrequire 35 bits to retain underflow. Expose quotient and remainder from\nthe same network; apply quotient sign from a_sign XOR b_sign and\nremainder sign from a_sign only for signed operations. Explicitly\noverride division by zero before sign correction: quotient is all ones\nand remainder is the original dividend. Preserve INT_MIN/-1 results.\nThis targets fewer serial quotient-selection stages and shared arithmetic\nto improve timing and routing area. Keep the combinationa\n…[41307 of 44379 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7ed35ae8571c0a0c]…\nintegration,\nforwarding and held operands, all branch and memory behavior, nret=1,\npublic IO and ordered RVFI retirement unchanged. Change no invariant,\ncorrectness assertion or ten-clock ready-bus progress bound.\n\nRemoving the serial radix-8-result-to-radix-4-subtraction dependency\nshould shorten the LOOP path despite a deeper final selection tree.\nExpected fitness gain is eight percent, unmeasured. The risks are\nextra divisor registers and subtractors, numerator fanout, PREP timing\nand the unchanged WB/branch bottleneck. Require vendor timing for all\nthree scored placements; at unchanged cycles acceptance needs median\nFmax above 83.683 MHz and fitness above 191.13558. A Python recurrence\nmodel matched independent unsigned division/remainder on 100225\nboundary/random pairs; this is arithmetic-model evidence, not RTL proof.\nRequire existing real/ALTOPS unit tests, complete formal and ready/stalled\nISS cosim gates, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation\nwith exactly 4378154 measured cycles.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
