{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_87", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r3s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r3s0',\n 'title':'Preserve ID/EX operand flops against register-file RAM absorption',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion reaches 47.33 MHz and fitness 105.38 with 4491485\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its 27.119 ns worst path runs from the\nregister file through ID, EX branch resolution, IF and hazard logic\nback to an ID operand register. Prior micro_opt radix-4 divider\nattempts reached only 6.277 and 39.675 MHz. The five-bit registered\ndivider has moved the bottleneck to ordinary operand/redirect logic.\nScratch Gowin reports show a clocked register-file BSRAM output\nfeeding ID operand muxes and EX directly, without an intervening\noperand flop on those paths. Preserving that existing pipeline\nboundary is a more focused response than changing instruction latency.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Make the two existing 32-bit ID/EX operand values explicit registers\nand preserve them as flip-flops in Gowin synthesis. The single\nmicro-optimization is to prevent operand-register absorption into\nregister-file RAM or equivalent sequential transformations that\nleave a long RF-read-to-EX-to-redirect cone. Do not add a pipeline\nstage or change any instruction's acceptance or execution clock.\n\nIn id_stage declare dedicated rs1_val_q and rs2_val_q registers with\nGowin's documented syn_preserve attribute. Route out.rs1_val and\nout.rs2_val from these registers rather than leaving operand state\ninside a large packed bundle whose fields the mapper can absorb.\nRetain the other bundle fields and the module's current interface.\nUse exactly the current operand transitions: reset or flush clears\nboth values; \"'!stall captures the two register-file read values;\nduring a hold, refresh a matching operand from valid nonzero WB\nwrites before its producer leaves the forwarding window. Preserve\nflush-before-stall priority and the original valid-register update.\nRemove the redundant operand fields from the bundle'\"'s internal state\nor tie them off before overriding the output, avoiding extra copies.\nThe attribute must change the timed circuit, not merely rename nodes.\n\nKeep all fetch NOP masking, hazard priorities, forwarding priority,\nbranch comparisons and redirect timing, register-file logical reset,\nand arithmetic exactly as in the champion. Keep the seven-iteration\nfive-bit divider, its launch/accept interface, held metadata, ALTOPS\nformulas and the unchanged ten-clock progress ceiling. This proposal\nhas no predictor, cache, wider retirement or additional latency.\n\nCheck the post-synthesis circuit and vendor timing report: both\noperand paths must cross an actual preserved register boundary.\nPreservation can increase flop count or prevent efficient RAM mapping;\naccept that only if the full timed circuit improves. The register\nfile's asynchronous reads may map differently as a consequence,\nbut do not separately redesign its storage or weaken reset behavior.\nDo not preserve unrelated RVFI payloads: they are verification-only\nand do not help the scored timing.\n\nAt the unchanged cycle count, the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold\nrequires median Fmax above 49.51 MHz. Expected improvement is about\n15 percent, with medium confidence pending vendor evaluation. The\nmain risks are RAM/read-mux area growth and another ALU or divider\npath becoming critical. Measure all three scored Gowin placement\noptions and compare median Fmax times the real marker-window\niterations/cycle; a circuit-neutral placement shift is insufficient.\n\nRun the original pipeline and real/ALTOPS core-divider tests, plus\nselftest and random full-trace cosim with ready and stalled buses.\nExercise writes into both source registers immediately before decode,\nEX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding, reset/flush coincident with holds,\nload-use bubbles, branch/JALR recovery and WB refresh during older\nmemory/divider stalls. Require precise RVFI operands, PC continuity,\nordered exact-once retirement and suppression of wrong-path stores.\nRetain the original formal suite and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC,\nUART, bounds and marker-window checks, nret=1 and every invariant.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':15,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Extract only the two ID/EX operand values into dedicated 32-bit\nregisters with Gowin syn_preserve attributes, and assemble the output\nbundle from those registers. Preserve every reset, flush, capture,\nhold and WB-refresh transition; avoid redundant operand state and\npreservation of verification-only metadata. Confirm the mapped\noperand register boundary and scored vendor timing.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all existing tests. Add directed source-value checks for\nsame-cycle WB/read collisions, simultaneous two-source forwarding,\nload-use bubbles and forwarded branch/JALR recovery under independent\nbus stalls. Check exact architectural results, PC/order continuity\nand no wrong-path retirement or stores.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_core_div.py','description':'''Preserve all real/ALTOPS arithmetic, source-refresh, held-result and\nten-clock progress assertions. Extend held ID/EX coverage where\nboth source writers leave WB during data/divider holds, plus flush\nand reset boundaries. Verify the preserved operand registers retain\nthe same logical values and retirement behavior.\n'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(f'Wrote and validated {p}')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
