{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && rg -n 'micro_opt|hyp-20261001-001-r3s0|hyp-20261001-002-r3s1|hyp-20261001-003-r3s2|mul|critical' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 (improvement, +462.46%): Replacing ALU `/` and `%` with four registered groups of eight restoring steps and separate magnitude/sign stages shortens the critical path enough to outweigh six-cycle DIV/REM latency in CoreMark's division-light timed kernels.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 (regression, +11.47%): A 64-entry folded-PC BHT plus direct JAL prediction raised CoreMark throughput 7.19% by avoiding EX flush bubbles, but the forwarded combinational DIV/REM path still limited Fmax to 5.66 MHz, making divider pipelining the higher-impact change.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r2s1 (improvement, +54.58%): Reducing div_unit's serial restoring steps per register from eight to five improves timing without increasing CoreMark's marker cycles, while folding magnitude/sign work into launch/accept edges preserves the ten-clock branch-to-DIV liveness bound despite seven LOOP clocks.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r2s2 (regression, +11.18%): A 64-entry BHT/JAL predictor with one-bit direction recovery removes CoreMark flush bubbles while retaining divider-limited timing, but eight serial restoring steps per divider clock leave Fmax at 31.76 MHz versus the five-step divider's 47.33 MHz.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 (improvement, +6.93%): Pairing a 64-entry BHT/JAL predictor with validity-only ID/EX recovery removes correct-prediction flush bubbles without routing EX redirects through instruction masking or wide payload enables, making prediction profitable on the five-step divider.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothe\n…[92050 of 95122 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2f9099f682cce0a3]…\ness\": 112.68, \"delta_pct\": 6.93, \"vs_baseline\": 829.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 47.218, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4190281, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3392, \"ff\": 780, \"seeds\": [45.508, 47.218, 47.218], \"perturbations\": [[0, 45.508, 17], [1, 47.218, 16], [2, 47.218, 16]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.974, \"arrival_ns\": 27.269, \"logic_cells\": 17, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 17, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T02:44:18.873999Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 (improvement, +6.93%): Pairing a 64-entry BHT/JAL predictor with validity-only ID/EX recovery removes correct-prediction flush bubbles without routing EX redirects through instruction masking or wide payload enables, making prediction profitable on the five-step divider.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
