{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n print('\\\\n',r['id'],r.get('category'),r.get('title'),r.get('outcome'),r.get('fitness'),r.get('fmax_mhz'))\n print('critical_path:', r.get('critical_path'))\n if r.get('category')=='micro_opt' or r['id'].endswith('r3s1'):\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('hypothesis:',h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('implementation_notes:',r.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n baseline-bench-4a6c0e6 micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench improvement 12.12 5.442\ncritical_path: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhypothesis: None\nimplementation_notes: \n\n hyp-20261001-001-r1s0 micro_opt Shared radix-4 combinational divider with borrow-based digit selection regression 13.98 6.277\ncritical_path: {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -156.85, 'arrival_ns': 167.145, 'logic_cells': 452, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhypothesis: Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one shared, fully\ncombinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divider. Convert operands to\nunsigned magnitudes for DIV and REM, and use the original bit patterns\nfor DIVU and REMU. Precompute widened divisor multiples B, 2B and 3B.\nUnroll 16 digit stages, consuming the dividend from its most significant\npair of bits to its least significant pair. At each stage form the\nwidened partial dividend P = 4*remainder + next_pair, calculate P-B,\nP-2B and P-3B in parallel, and select the largest nonnegative trial to\nemit quotient digit 0, 1, 2 or 3 and the corresponding new remainder.\nDerive trial validity from each widened subtraction's borrow bit rather\nthan instantiating a separate magnitude comparator followed by another\nsubtraction. Use sufficient unsigned width throughout: divisor\nmultiples and partial dividends require 34 bits, and trial differences\nrequire 35 bits to retain underflow. Expose quotient and remainder from\nthe same network; apply quotient sign from a_sign XOR b_sign and\nremainder sign from a_sign only for signed operations. Explicitly\noverride division by zero before sign correction: quotient is all ones\nand remainder is the original dividend. Preserve INT_MIN/-1 results.\nThis targets fewer serial quotient-selection stages and shared arithme\n…[11384 of 14456 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:465c4a67b16f7dee]…\nine-control restructuring, with no predictor, cache,\nnew arithmetic algorithm or extra pipeline stage. Leave the seven\nfive-bit divider iterations, multiply hardware, decoder legality and\nALTOPS formulas unchanged. Preserve nret=1, public IO and all checks.\nReady-bus branch/JAL/JALR-to-DIV retirement spacing must remain at most\nten clocks; ordinary retirement timing and stalled CoreMark cycles\nshould remain unchanged. Validate with the unchanged formal suite,\ninstruction-stream cosim, canonical CRCs and vendor median timing.\nThe expected gain comes entirely from removing a long control path;\nthe shortened divider or ALU may become the next timing limit.\n\nimplementation_notes: \n\n hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 predictor Compact bimodal prediction with validity-only recovery improvement 112.68 47.218\ncritical_path: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -16.974, 'arrival_ns': 27.269, 'logic_cells': 17, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
