{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r4s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261001-001-r4s0\ntitle: \"Flatten execute operand selection with exclusive one-hot bypass enables\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 112.68 at 47.218 MHz. Its reported worst path starts\n  at a WB destination register and crosses ID, EX and the ALU before a\n  memory-side endpoint. The five-step registered divider has already\n  removed the original dominant arithmetic bottleneck. The previous\n  micro_opt attempt to preserve ID/EX operand flops regressed by 1.81\n  percent, so this proposal targets actual operand-selection logic.\n  Current EX first selects a register source using an encoded bypass\n  selector, then applies separate PC/immediate operand muxes. Reducing\n  this serial selection depth can raise Fmax without changing CoreMark\n  cycles or the successful predictor and divider behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the encoded EX forwarding selectors and subsequent ALU-source\n  mux cascade with mutually exclusive one-hot operand enables. Compute\n  EX/MEM and MEM/WB register matches once per source in forward_unit,\n  retaining valid reg_write qualification, nonzero destinations and\n  strict EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB-over-ID/EX priority. Export three enables\n  per source: ex_hit, !ex_hit && wb_hit, and !ex_hit && !wb_hit.\n  Construct each raw forwarded rs value with a masked bitwise OR of\n  its three sources. Do not introduce a priority case or encoded\n  selector followed by another decode at the 32-bit datapath.\n\n  Independently form the ALU operands directly from the same source\n  buses, folding the existing PC and immediate overrides into their\n  enables. For operand A, select PC when is_auipc, otherwise enable\n  exactly one register/bypass source. For operand B, select the\n  immediate when alu_src, otherwise enable exactly one register/bypass\n  source. The ALU input must not pass through the raw forwarded rs mux\n  before a second PC/immediate mux. These expressions must remain\n  equivalent for every control combination, including invalid held\n  payloads. Keep raw forwarded rs1/rs2 for comp\n…[1759 of 4831 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:43436658a6384f0b]…\norm raw rs values with\n      masked OR selection and form ALU operands independently with\n      PC/immediate overrides folded into the source enables, eliminating\n      serial forwarding-then-operand muxes. Preserve every branch,\n      store, divider, stall and RVFI use of the raw forwarded sources.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the wider internal one-hot bypass controls between the\n      forwarding and execute units. Preserve all top-level ports,\n      producer eligibility, pipeline controls and retirement behavior.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing assertions and add directed sequences covering\n      both bypass ages, simultaneous matching writers, x0, ALU register\n      and immediate operands, AUIPC, branch/JALR and store sources.\n      Under independent bus stalls verify architectural operand values,\n      exact-once ordered retirement and held WB operand refresh. Require\n      existing divider, ALU, formal and canonical stalled CoreMark gates.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
