action's borrow bit rather\nthan instantiating a separate magnitude comparator followed by another\nsubtraction. Use sufficient unsigned width throughout: divisor\nmultiples and partial dividends require 34 bits, and trial differences\nrequire 35 bits to retain underflow. Expose quotient and remainder from\nthe same network; apply quotient sign from a_sign XOR b_sign and\nremainder sign from a_sign only for signed operations. Explicitly\noverride division by zero before sign correction: quotient is all ones\nand remainder is the original dividend. Preserve INT_MIN/-1 results.\nThis targets fewer serial quotient-selection stages and shared arithmetic\nto improve timing and routing ar\n…[10309 of 13381 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:041d736a4c6805e3]…\nea changed from 3392 LUT/780 FF to 3396 LUT/\n812 FF, with the same eight LUT-RAMs, six BSRAMs and six DSPs.\nThe worst path now ends at EX/MEM.alu_result rather than a memory\naddress port. This is a circuit change, not a rename or preservation\nattribute. The prototype passed all 18 existing pipeline tests and\nseven core-divider tests in each of real and ALTOPS modes. Selftest\nand all three random instruction ELFs passed full RVFI cosimulation\nboth with ready buses and with independent instruction/data stalls.\nCanonical stalled CoreMark passed CRC, UART, bounds and timing-marker\nvalidation, completing ten iterations in exactly 4190281 bracketed\ncycles, unchanged from the champion. Combining this throughput with\nmeasured median Fmax yields prototype fitness 120.35 versus 112.68,\nabove the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold. Full formal remains an\nimplementation gate; rerun the unchanged correctness and scored\ntiming gates on the implemented candidate. Routing of other nearly\ncritical paths remains a risk.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
