{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_76", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r5s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261001-001-r5s0\ntitle: \\\"Compact Boolean divider seed with direct magnitude-nibble extraction\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 124.78 at median 54.63 MHz and 4378154 CoreMark\n  marker cycles. An unchanged vendor run reproduces its 24.469 ns worst\n  path from the register file through ID and EX into divider remainder_q.\n  Launch currently chains full-width signed magnitude conversion and\n  four dependent restoring steps for a numerator of only four bits.\n  Earlier full-width radix-4, operand preservation and dedicated address\n  micro-optimizations did not beat the later champions. Optimize this\n  bounded launch calculation without changing instruction latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the divider's real-arithmetic launch seed with a compact\n  combinational Boolean network. Keep the existing IDLE/LOOP/DONE state\n  machine, seven four-bit restoring LOOP clocks, signed correction,\n  exceptions, start/busy/done/accept and EX integration unchanged.\n\n  Let neg_a=signed_op && a[31] and neg_b=signed_op && b[31]. Extract the\n  four-bit magnitude numerator N directly from forwarded raw a. If\n  neg_a is false, N=a[31:28]. Otherwise N=(~a[31:28]+(a[27:0]==0))\n  modulo 16. A reduction tree and four-bit increment implement the exact\n  two's-complement identity without placing a 32-bit carry chain before\n  the seed. Retain the existing full-width magnitude_a for the lower\n  28 dividend bits captured into quotient_q.\n\n  Classify magnitude_b<16 directly from raw b. For neg_b=false require\n  b[31:4]==0. For neg_b=true require b[31:4]==28'hfffffff AND b[3:0]\"'!=0:\n  exactly -1 through -15 qualify, while -16 and larger magnitudes do not.\n  The seed divisor D is b[3:0] or its four-bit negation according to\n  neg_b. Keep full-width magnitude_b capture into divisor_q unchanged.\n\n  For D=1..7, calculate {floor(N/D),N%D} with constant Boolean truth\n  masks. For each divisor and each of eight output bits, embed a 16-bit\n  constant whose bit N is that exact quotient/remainder output bit.\n  Index each constant by N, gate its eight-bit result with the shared\n  three-bit equality D[2:0]==divisor, and combine the eight gated terms\n  with a balanced OR. D=0 can deterministically return quotient zero\n  and remainder N because the existing architectural zero-divisor\n  override remains authoritative. Generate constants when writing RTL;\n  introduce no runtime division, remainder or multiplication operators.\n\n  For D=8..15, the quotient is at most one. Calculate one unsigned\n  five-bit trial T={1'\"'b0,N}-{1'b0,D}; quotient is {3'b0,\"'!T[4]} and\n  remainder is T[4] ? N : T[3:0]. Select this pair when D[3] is set;\n  otherwise use the small-divisor Boolean result. For magnitude_b>=16,\n  override the pair with quotient zero and remainder N. Capture exactly\n  quotient_q={magnitude_a[27:0],seed_quotient} and\n  remainder_q={28'\"'b0,seed_remainder}. Remove all four serial seed steps.\n\n  Implement the truth masks as combinational constant-bit selections\n  and shared divisor decoding, rather than a 256-entry clocked case ROM.\n  A scratch case-table prototype inferred an extra BSRAM and regressed.\n  A logic-only full-table prototype kept six BSRAMs and 982 flops,\n  passed existing real/ALTOPS divider and core pipeline tests, and reached\n  median 56.409 MHz; its worst paths moved to branch recovery/training.\n  That measured 3.26 percent timing gain is below the 4.6 percent bar.\n  This compact form halves the Boolean table's divisor fanout and uses\n  one small parallel trial for its upper half, aiming to reduce routing\n  and close the remaining timing gap. Do not claim the full-table result\n  alone meets acceptance. Evaluate this exact compact circuit.\n\n  Preserve all ALTOPS formulas and timing, full RV32M bit results,\n  divisor-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling, frozen DONE outputs, reset,\n  bus stalls, WB refresh, nret=1 and every decoder/RVFI invariant.\n  At unchanged marker cycles, acceptance needs median Fmax above\n  57.143 MHz and fitness above 130.52. Expected gain is 6 percent with\n  medium confidence. Main risks are branch or LOOP paths becoming the\n  new limit and FPGA inference/routing offsetting the seed improvement.\n  Require unchanged formal, liveness, stalled cosim and canonical\n  CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker-window gates on the implementation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace serial launch seed arithmetic with direct signed magnitude\n      nibble extraction, raw-operand small-divisor classification, eight\n      sets of constant Boolean truth masks and one five-bit upper-half\n      trial subtraction. Preserve full-width operand capture, seven\n      four-step restoring LOOP cycles, all exceptions, DONE correction\n      and the exact real/ALTOPS handshake and reset behavior.\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing arithmetic and handshake assertion. Cover\n      every numerator nibble and divisor magnitude 1..15 for all signed\n      operand combinations, negative -16/-17 classification boundaries,\n      zero, INT_MIN and high unsigned divisors. Exercise lower-28-bit\n      zero/one/maximum patterns at magnitude-nibble carry boundaries.\n      Compare exact results with independent integer division truncated\n      toward zero; assert unchanged latency, ignored busy requests,\n      stable held completion, acceptance and reset cancellation.\n''')\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261001-001-r5s0' and h['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Schema-valid final hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
