.sv are the\\nstrongest candidate for this deep arithmetic path. CoreMark fitness\\nscales directly with Fmax when instruction latency and cycle count stay\\nconstant. There are no earlier bench hypotheses or recorded lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one shared, fully\\ncombinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divider. Convert operands to\\nunsigned magn\n…[48072 of 51144 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:071df5457fc6c749]…\nment\", \"fitness\": 134.9, \"delta_pct\": 8.11, \"vs_baseline\": 1013.04, \"fmax_mhz\": 59.061, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4378154, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4091, \"ff\": 1147, \"seeds\": [57.266, 59.061, 59.061], \"perturbations\": [[0, 57.266, 16], [1, 59.061, 15], [2, 59.061, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -12.462, \"arrival_ns\": 22.757, \"logic_cells\": 16, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T03:59:58.741432Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r5s1 (improvement, +8.11%): Consuming five quotient bits per LOOP with parallel radix-8/radix-4 trials frees a PREP clock for preserved raw-operand registers, shortening the forwarding-to-divider path while preserving DIV/REM latency and CoreMark marker cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
