{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt':\n  print(d['id'], d.get('title'), d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'), d.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  if 'r3s0' in d['id'] or 'r4s0' in d['id']:\n   print(json.dumps(d,indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-4a6c0e6 Baseline retest for cores/bench improvement 12.12 5.442\nhyp-20261001-001-r1s0 Shared radix-4 combinational divider with borrow-based digit selection regression 13.98 6.277\nhyp-20261001-001-r2s0 Parallel radix-4 digit selection inside the registered divider regression 88.33 39.675\nhyp-20261001-001-r3s0 Preserve ID/EX operand flops against register-file RAM absorption regression 103.47 46.475\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261001-001-r3s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Preserve ID/EX operand flops against register-file RAM absorption\",\n  \"category\": \"micro_opt\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion reaches 47.33 MHz and fitness 105.38 with 4491485\\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its 27.119 ns worst path runs from the\\nregister file through ID, EX branch resolution, IF and hazard logic\\nback to an ID operand register. Prior micro_opt radix-4 divider\\nattempts reached only 6.277 and 39.675 MHz. The five-bit registered\\ndivider has moved the bottleneck to ordinary operand/redirect logic.\\nScratch Gowin reports show a clocked register-file BSRAM output\\nfeeding ID operand muxes and EX directly, without an intervening\\noperand flop on those paths. Preserving that existing pipeline\\nboundary is a more focused response than changing instruction latency.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The champion reaches 47.33 MHz and fitness 105.38 with 4491485\\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its 27.119 ns worst path runs from the\\nregister file through ID, EX branch re