{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_77", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git status --short; cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r6s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261001-001-r6s0\ntitle: Share logical and arithmetic right shifts through one signed barrel\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 134.90 at median 59.061 MHz and 4378154 CoreMark\n  marker cycles. Its worst vendor path runs from the register file\n  through ID, forwarding and the ordinary ALU to a data-memory address\n  register, with 22.757 ns arrival and 16 cells. Divider retiming has\n  removed the previous launch bottleneck. The detailed path carries\n  operand bit 27 to a low memory-address bit through the shift/result\n  network, so a shorter ADD carry chain alone cannot fix it. The ALU\n  currently expresses SRL and SRA as separate variable shifts followed\n  by operation selection. Sharing their barrel directly targets this\n  ordinary datapath without adding pipeline clocks.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only SRL/SRA computation in alu.sv with a shared combinational\n  signed 33-bit right barrel. Form an explicitly signed operand\n  right_input = $signed({(op == ALU_SRA) && a[31], a}). Compute one\n  signed result right_shifted = right_input >>> b[4:0], then return\n  right_shifted[31:0] for both ALU_SRL and ALU_SRA. Keep the left shifter\n  and every other ALU result expression and operation encoding unchanged.\n  Declare both intermediate signals signed; an unsigned concatenation\n  or unsigned shift would silently break negative arithmetic shifts.\n\n  The extra top bit is zero for SRL and copies a[31] for SRA. Consequently\n  one arithmetic shift gives exactly the required zero fill or sign fill\n  in the low 32 result bits, for every shift amount 0 through 31. Use\n  b[4:0] alone, including for immediate shift encodings; upper b bits\n  must have no effect. This removes separate logical/arithmetic shift\n  results and their late selection while preserving combinational timing\n  and the complete 32-bit architectural result. Do not merge SLL with\n  the right barrel or add bit-reversal muxes.\n\n  This is one local ALU sharing micro-optimization. Add no register,\n  execution clock, prediction feature, stor\n…[1681 of 4753 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d04fce9487cda59a]…\nounds and marker-window checks on the implemented candidate.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n- file: rtl/alu.sv\n  description: |\n    Add explicitly signed 33-bit right_input and right_shifted signals.\n    Prefix a with the SRA-qualified sign bit and compute one arithmetic\n    right shift by b[4:0]. Route both SRL and SRA case arms to its low\n    32 bits. Retain SLL and every other operation verbatim, with the\n    original combinational interface and execution latency.\n- file: test/test_alu.py\n  description: |\n    Retain every existing check. Independently verify SRL and SRA for\n    all 32 shift amounts using zero, all ones, signed extrema, every\n    single-bit and single-clear-bit operand, alternating patterns and\n    deterministic randomized operands. Vary upper shift-operand bits\n    and switch consecutively between SRL/SRA/SLL to detect signedness,\n    control or masking regressions. Run existing pipeline, formal and\n    stalled CoreMark gates with no assertion weakened.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
