{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id')=='hyp-20261001-003-r5s2':\n  h=d['hypothesis']; print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Preserve the successful 64x2-bit folded-PC bimodal predictor, but replace\nits reset-all counter implementation with FPGA distributed LUT RAM and\none serialized cold-initialization controller. This is one predictor\nstorage change; retain the current raw legal-branch/JAL predecode,\ndirect-target arithmetic, speculation bounds and alignment checks,\npredicted_taken metadata, direct one-bit EX verification, validity-only\nrecovery and sequential JALR policy.\n\nRemove reset assignment from the counter array. Reset only a seven-bit\ninitialization count to zero. On each non-reset edge while count[6] is\nzero, write 2'b01 to counters[count[5:0]] and increment the count. The\nedge that writes entry 63 changes the count to 64; then hold it at 64\nuntil reset. Predict conditional branches sequentially during these\n64 cold-start clocks, and discard conditional-branch training during\ninitialization because the single RAM write port belongs to the sweep.\nDirect JAL prediction remains active throughout initialization. The\nsweep must run independently of fetch stalls, dmem stalls and M holds;\nit must never stall the CPU or alter architectural next-PC resolution.\nReset restarts the entire sweep, including if it interrupts a sweep.\n\nAfter initialization, use the exact current index PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]\nfor both lookup and training, the same weakly-not-taken state, and\nold-counter simultaneous read/write semantics. Fetch needs the direction\nMSB at fetch_index; training reads the complete old counter at train_index.\nInfer asynchronous distributed RAM with one clocked write port; Gowin\nmay replicate the small RAM to provide the two independent read ports.\nUse portable inference and a distributed-RAM synthesis hint rather than\ninstantiating vendor primitives that cannot run through Verilator and\nriscv-formal. No unknown RAM bit may affect prediction before all entries\nare initialized, including repeated or partial resets.\n\nExpress the training transition with two small Boolean functions and\nwrite on every qualified train_valid, including saturation. For old\nstate {d,h}, increment yields {d|h, d|~h}, and decrement yields\n{d&h, d&~h}. These exactly implement 00/01/10/11 two-bit saturation,\neliminating indexed conditional write-enable and increment/decrement\narithmetic. Preserve EX's existing valid/legal/non-trapping/advancing\ntraining qualifications and do not add an EX-to-IF lookup bypass.\n\nThe intended physical result is RAM counter storage, approximately\n120 fewer counter/control flip-flops if the original table used flops,\nand less reset and write-decoder routing. Timing improvement must come\nfrom that real circuit change. The current worst path lies in divider\nlaunch, so a six percent fitness gain remains low-confidence until\nmeasured; do not claim direction-accuracy or steady-state IPC gains.\nCoreMark begins its timed window after more than ten thousand retired\ninitialization instructions, well after the fixed 64-clock sweep.\nCold-start changes can shift the pseudo-random stall phase, so measure\nactual marker cycles rather than assuming bit-identical cycle counts.\n\nKeep nret=1 and every external port, decoder/trap invariant, load-use\nbehavior, held WB refresh, M arithmetic/lifecycle, recovery-over-stall\npriority and ordered exact-once RVFI retirement unchanged. Test all\neight counter transitions, independent fetch/train addresses, aliases,\nsame-edge old-value reads, saturation writes, interrupted reset sweeps\nand training attempts during initialization. Exercise direct JAL and\nbranch recovery throughout warmup under independent bus stalls. Require\nunchanged correctness gates and canonical CRC/UART/MMIO bounds; accept\nonly measured vendor median Fmax times actual iterations/cycle above\n130.52 iterations/second. Check that synthesis really reduces counter\nregisters and maps the array into LUT RAM; an unchanged netlist is not\nevidence for this hypothesis.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
