{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261001-002-r7s1','hyp-20261001-001-r6s0']:\n  print(r['id'])\n  print(json.dumps(r['critical_path'],indent=2))\n  print('NOTES',r.get('implementation_notes',''))\n  if '001-r6s0' in r['id']: print(json.dumps(r['hypothesis'],indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-001-r6s0\n{\n  \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\n  \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\",\n  \"slack_ns\": -11.384,\n  \"arrival_ns\": 21.679,\n  \"logic_cells\": 14,\n  \"modules\": [\n    \"clock_ibuf\",\n    \"cpu/u_id\",\n    \"cpu/u_ex\",\n    \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n    \"cpu/u_ex\"\n  ]\n}\nNOTES \n{\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 134.90 at median 59.061 MHz and 4378154 CoreMark\\nmarker cycles. Its worst vendor path runs from the register file\\nthrough ID, forwarding and the ordinary ALU to a data-memory address\\nregister, with 22.757 ns arrival and 16 cells. Divider retiming has\\nremoved the previous launch bottleneck. The detailed path carries\\noperand bit 27 to a low memory-address bit through the shift/result\\nnetwork, so a shorter ADD carry chain alone cannot fix it. The ALU\\ncurrently expresses SRL and SRA as separate variable shifts followed\\nby operation selection. Sharing their barrel directly targets this\\nordinary datapath without adding pipeline clocks.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only SRL/SRA computation in alu.sv with a shared combinational\\nsigned 33-bit right barrel. Form an explicitly signed operand\\nright_input = $signed({(op == ALU_SRA) && a[31], a}). Compute one\\nsigned result right_shifted = right_input >>> b[4:0], then return\\nright_shifted[31:0] for both ALU_SRL and ALU_SRA. Keep the left shifter\\nand every other ALU result expression and operation encoding unchanged.\\nDeclare both intermediate signals signed; an unsigned concatenation\\nor unsigned shift would silently break negative arithmetic shifts.\\n\\nThe extra top bit is zero for SRL and copies a[31] for SRA. Consequently\\none arithmetic shift gives exactly the required zero fill or sign fill\\nin the low 32 result bits, for every shift amount 0 through 31. Use\\nb[4:0] alone, including for immediate shift encodings; upper b bits\\nmust have no effect. This removes separate logical/arithmetic shift\\nresults and their late selection while preserving combinational timing\\nand the complete 32-bit architectural result. Do not merge SLL with\\nthe right barrel \n…[2146 of 5218 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:db22cf55ae5c2270]…\ntic\\nright shift by b[4:0]. Route both SRL and SRA case arms to its low\\n32 bits. Retain SLL and every other operation verbatim, with the\\noriginal combinational interface and execution latency.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Retain every existing check. Independently verify SRL and SRA for\\nall 32 shift amounts using zero, all ones, signed extrema, every\\nsingle-bit and single-clear-bit operand, alternating patterns and\\ndeterministic randomized operands. Vary upper shift-operand bits\\nand switch consecutively between SRL/SRA/SLL to detect signedness,\\ncontrol or masking regressions. Run existing pipeline, formal and\\nstalled CoreMark gates with no assertion weakened.\\n\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nhyp-20261001-002-r7s1\n{\n  \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_10_s0\",\n  \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_9_s1\",\n  \"slack_ns\": -10.003,\n  \"arrival_ns\": 20.298,\n  \"logic_cells\": 32,\n  \"modules\": [\n    \"clock_ibuf\",\n    \"cpu/u_id\",\n    \"cpu/u_ex\",\n    \"cpu/u_id\",\n    \"cpu/u_ex\",\n    \"cpu/u_if\"\n  ]\n}\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
