{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_84", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r9s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261001-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Single parallel radix-32 digit per existing divider LOOP clock\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 174.65 at 76.466 MHz. Its two serial radix-8 and\n  radix-4 trial/subtract/select networks consume five quotient bits per\n  LOOP edge. Recent timing improvements to branch recovery repeatedly\n  expose this divider recurrence at approximately 19 ns arrival and\n  70 cells. Earlier radix-4 and radix-8 trials show that parallel borrow\n  decisions are useful, but the current network still propagates two\n  full-width subtract/select decisions within one register interval.\n  Remove that remaining serial arithmetic without changing latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only div_unit's real-arithmetic LOOP datapath with one fully\n  parallel radix-32 digit. Preserve raw launch, PREP, the two-bit seed,\n  exactly six LOOP edges, DONE/accept, sign correction and all ALTOPS\n  behavior. There is no new architectural pipeline stage or clock.\n\n  For a nonzero unsigned magnitude divisor D and current remainder R,\n  form the 37-bit numerator U = {remainder_q, quotient_q[31:27]}.\n  Register the explicitly widened 37-bit multiples k*D, k=1..31, during\n  the existing PREP edge. Compute all 38-bit differences\n  {1'b0,U} - {1'b0,multiple_q[k]} concurrently. Let fit[k] be the\n  inverse of bit 37, the unsigned underflow indicator. The monotonic\n  trial flags select exactly one digit: select[0]=!fit[1],\n  select[k]=fit[k]&&!fit[k+1] for k=1..30, select[31]=fit[31].\n  Encode five quotient bits with parallel masked-OR reductions of\n  these one-hot selects. Append them with\n  quotient_next={quotient_q[26:0],digit}. Select U or the corresponding\n  trial residual with a balanced 32-leaf masked-OR tree, retaining its\n  low 32 bits as remainder_next. Avoid a 31-arm priority mux.\n\n  For D>0, R<D implies U<32*D, so the largest fitting digit is 0..31\n  and the restored residual is below D. Six five-bit LOOP clocks plus\n  the unchanged two-bit seed consume precisely 32 dividend bits.\n  Never truncate the \n…[2894 of 5966 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8c2d0620478a9b71]…\nmerator, 31 parallel 38-bit trials, borrow-derived\n      one-hot digit selection, balanced residual tree and five-bit\n      quotient append. Generate and capture exact 37-bit divisor\n      multiples with constant shifts, widened add/subtract and\n      carry-save networks in the existing PREP clock. Preserve seed,\n      FSM, raw registers, latency, reset, exceptions, correction,\n      start/busy/done/accept interface and ALTOPS formulas verbatim.\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every current arithmetic, seed, handshake, reset, hold\n      and exact-latency assertion. Extend directed tests to k*D-1,\n      k*D and k*D+1 for all digit thresholds 1..31, including large\n      divisors and widened preparation carries. Add deterministic\n      random bit-pattern operands and verify all four operations\n      against independent Python division with truncation toward\n      zero. Require existing pipeline/M progress, ready/stalled\n      cosim, canonical CoreMark and unchanged formal gates.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
