4, qualified by\n  no reset/recovery. Head consumption requires head_available and\n  no downstream hold. An incoming instruction consumed through empty\n  fall-through advances fetch without entering storage. Otherwise an\n  accepted fetch appends at occupancy minus any simultaneous queued\n  pop. A queued pop shifts slots 1..3 toward fixed slot zero; a\n  simultaneous append overrides the vacated tail. Occupancy changes\n  by stored_push minus queued_pop. Distinguish fall-through consumption\n  from storage dequeue. Use compile-time fixed slot assignments with\n  decoded append enables; do not infer variable-index storage, RAM\n  or a circular head mux. When full, decline physical fetch for that\n  edge even if a queued head pops, keeping fetch admission dependent\n  on registered occupancy alone. Head issue still proceeds. States\n  zero through three sustain simultaneous fetch and issue when allowed.\n\n  Advance fetch on physical acceptance during load-use, data-memory\n  and M holds, filling available slots. Never advance or enqueue while\n  io_imemReady=0. Buffered heads can issue during physical bus stalls.\n  RF read addresses and load-use tags come from the current queue head,\n  and hazard instruction availability comes from head_available.\n  Decode/RF reads and registered forwarding choices occur on actual\n  head consumption; do not prefetch operand values or forwarding tags.\n  Preserve existing data/M holds, held WB refresh and load-use bubbles.\n\n  EX recovery overrides all frontend holds and physical bus stalls.\n  On the existing recovery edge, discard all queued and incoming\n  wrong-path tokens, clear occupancy, invalidate younger ID/EX and\n  set physical fetch PC to the existing correction target. Empty\n  fall-through presents a ready target on the following cycle: no\n  extra redirect register or recovery clock. Reset restores PC zero\n  and empty state. Reproduce the measured prototype'\"'s synchronous\n  clearing of all four slot payloads