{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] == 'hyp-20261001-003-r8s2':\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  for k in ['outcome','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','seeds','critical_path']: print(k,d.get(k))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replace the nested EX redirect-target and IF redirect/hold/prediction\narbitration with direction-specific recovery rails feeding the existing\nsingle full-width fetch-PC register. Preserve the 64-entry folded-PC\nbimodal predictor and its exact decisions, direct JAL prediction,\nsequential JALR prediction, pipeline schedule and all arithmetic units.\n\nDecode correction eligibility before the forwarded branch condition is\navailable. At the existing ID/EX capture boundary, register compact\nprequalifiers for an aligned legal direct transfer predicted sequential,\na legal conditional branch predicted taken, and a legal JALR. These\nbits are part of the accepted instruction payload, hold with it and are\nindependently qualified by EX validity, reset, older memory holds and\nM ownership. Direct alignment can be established from PC/immediate low\nbits independently of branch operands. Do not relax decoder validation\nor treat reserved branch/JALR encodings as control transfers.\n\nIn EX expose separate correction enables and unselected candidates:\ntaken direct correction with the raw full-width PC-relative target;\nnot-taken correction with PC+4; and aligned JALR correction with the\nforwarded rs1+immediate target after clearing bit zero. A taken direct\nbranch rail combines its registered prequalifier with branch_cond;\nits not-taken rail combines the predicted-taken prequalifier with\n!branch_cond. JAL is unconditional and JALR retains the existing\noperand-dependent alignment check. Illegal or misaligned transfers\npreserve existing trap/link/PC semantics. The correction enables must\nbe mutually exclusive and their OR must equal the original qualified\nredirect for every instruction, including invalid retained payloads.\n\nThe tested prequalifiers are precisely:\nD = !dec_is_illegal && !in.predicted_taken &&\n    (dec_is_branch || (dec_is_jump && !dec_is_jalr)) &&\n    ((in.pc[1:0] + imm[1:0]) modulo 4 == 0);\nF = !dec_is_illegal && dec_is_branch && in.predicted_taken;\nR = !dec_is_illegal && dec_is_jalr.\nRegister these on the existing ID payl\n…[3752 of 6824 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a56775ee00fc15b9]…\ntion-0 worst path is now divider recurrence,\n18.794 ns; option 1 also places WB-to-fetch near that limit at 18.582 ns.\nThis computes to 171.853 iterations/second, 6.87 percent above 160.81,\nexceeding the acceptance margin. All 53 checks generated from the\nunchanged single-issue formal configuration passed, including liveness,\nill, unique, cover and PC continuity. The IF predictor tests also passed\nwith the new internal inputs; additional pipeline/M assertions confirmed\nmutual exclusion and equality to the original actual_transfer XOR\npredicted_taken redirect under the existing advance qualifications.\nThese are prototype results; require fresh correctness gates and\nevaluator timing after implementation.\n\noutcome regression\nfitness 171.85\nfmax_mhz 75.24\ncycles 4378154\nseeds [74.077, 75.24, 75.24]\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_m/u_div/remainder_q_0_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_m/u_div/remainder_q_10_s1', 'slack_ns': -8.499, 'arrival_ns': 18.794, 'logic_cells': 71, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_m/u_div']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
