{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r12s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261001-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Register the final writeback value before operand feedback\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 182.73 at 80.002 MHz with 4378154 timed CoreMark\n  cycles. The r7s1 operand-delivery restructuring succeeded, but the\n  remaining feedback still selects between separately registered load\n  and scalar results after MEM/WB. Recent r11s0 and r11s2 worst paths\n  originate at MEM/WB mem_to_reg, and r11s1 originates at read_data and\n  ends at an EX ALU-result register. Split fetch-PC state and predictor\n  feedback changes did not clear the acceptance margin. These results\n  suggest removing result-class arbitration at the source of writeback\n  feedback rather than adding another frontend structure. No recorded\n  structural attempt has moved the final writeback mux across MEM/WB.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the two separately registered functional MEM/WB values plus\n  the post-register mem_to_reg mux with one preserved 32-bit final\n  writeback-value register at the existing MEM/WB edge. Select between\n  the fully extracted/sign-extended load result and EX/MEM scalar result\n  on the D side of that register. The scalar input already includes\n  ALU, jump-link and completed M results. Drive the RF write data, both\n  EX writeback-forwarding inputs, held-ID operand refresh and RVFI\n  rd_wdata from this registered value without further result-class\n  selection. This is one structural retiming of the writeback feedback\n  boundary; it adds no pipeline stage or instruction latency.\n\n  Give the functional value its own explicit register with narrowly\n  scoped Gowin preservation attributes, following the existing operand\n  and M-unit register style. Preserve the existing metadata and exact\n  MEM/WB validity/write eligibility. On hold_wb retain the value while\n  clearing retirement validity exactly as today: EX may still consume\n  that retained data through an already registered forwarding selector,\n  even though the corresponding WB token no longer writes or retires.\n  Reset initialize\n…[2774 of 5846 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:65b55a9179af675c]…\nnal registered MEM/WB value,\n      eliminating post-register mem_to_reg selection. Preserve w_en and\n      destination semantics so RF, EX forwarding, ID refresh and RVFI\n      automatically share the same correctly aligned registered result.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Update internal MEM/WB observations for the new representation\n      while retaining architectural assertions and independent expected\n      results. Exercise load widths and signs, load-to-ALU/branch/store,\n      scalar/load writer precedence, WB collisions and held operands\n      across instruction/data stalls; retain exact-once retirement and\n      stable stalled memory-request checks.\n  - file: test/test_core_div.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt internal result-field observations if needed and retain all\n      real/ALTOPS arithmetic references, exact-once M completion and\n      nine-/ten-clock ready-bus progress checks. Cover mixed load, scalar\n      and M result feedback with an older stalled memory request.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
