sion\",\n  \"fitness\": 103.85,\n  \"delta_pct\": -1.45,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 46.646,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -16.208,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 26.503,\n    \"logic_cells\": 13,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r4s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Retimed M-extension execution with registered multiply and seeded divide\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 124.78,\n  \"delta_pct\": 10.74,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 54.63,\n  \"cycles\": 4378154,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_m/u_div/remainder_q_0_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -14.174,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 24.469,\n    \"logic_cells\": 25,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n     \n…[17568 of 20640 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a10147266668658d]…\nory/M-unit behavior, RVFI fields and every correctness gate.\n\nValidate against an independent full-width pc+sign_extended_imm\nreference, concentrating on ten-bit block carry boundaries, twenty-bit\nwrap, negative offsets, bounds endpoints, misalignment, both immediate\nformats, all legal/reserved branch funct3 values, and high-PC wrap\ncases. Retain queue and pipeline recovery assertions, wrong-path\nstore/M suppression, and all existing progress bounds. Require\nunchanged formal/cosim/CoreMark CRC, UART, bounds and marker checks.\n\nThe expected gain is about seven percent through Fmax, without cycle\nsavings. At 4095164 cycles the 4.6 percent threshold requires roughly\n82.862 MHz median vendor Fmax and fitness above 202.33824 iter/sec.\nConfirm with Gowin timing that neither opcode-before-target addition\nnor a 32-bit carry-to-bounds chain remains. Carry-select duplication\nmay increase LU