{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261001-002-r3s1','hyp-20261001-002-r11s1','hyp-20261001-002-r14s1']:\n  h=r['hypothesis']\n  print(r['id'])\n  print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('CHANGES',json.dumps(r['changes'],indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-002-r3s1\nReplace frontend flushing by a separate instruction-validity control\nplane. Keep the existing pipeline register boundaries and single-issue\nexecution, but let fetched instruction bits and decoded payload travel\nindependently of the squash token. IF emits the raw imem instruction\neven when invalid; redirect and imem-not-ready suppress validity, not\nthe 32-bit instruction bus. Feed the load-use comparator from these raw\nfetched source fields and the valid ID/EX LOAD. A legal instruction in\nEX cannot be both LOAD and a redirecting branch/jump, so redirect need\nnot propagate through fetch NOP selection to recompute that hazard.\n\nIn ID/EX, split the valid flop update from payload-register updates.\nReset may still clear the payload. Flush must clear only valid, never\nsynchronously zero the operands, immediate, control, instruction and\nPC fields. Capture payload when the normal load-use/data-stall/divider\nhold allows advancement; refresh held operands from valid writeback\nexactly as today. Update valid with explicit reset/flush/hold/capture\npriority. During a load-use bubble the old payload may remain while\nvalid is zero; during a redirect a wrong-path payload may be captured\nbut must remain invalid. Do not mask the raw fetch instruction or\nreintroduce redirect into payload capture enables as a substitute.\n\nKeep redirect as a direct kill input to the ID/EX valid flop and as\nthe existing priority input to the PC register. Preserve frontend\nhold versus bubble behavior under independent instruction/data stalls\nand divider ownership. Qualify every architectural consumer of stale\npayload with validity: load-use detection, divider launch, forwarding\nproducer eligibility, redirects, memory enables, register writes and\nretirement. Preserve the current EX/MEM and MEM/WB validity discipline,\nexact-once stalled requests, held divider metadata and operand refresh.\nInvalid tokens may carry arbitrary decoded bits but cannot generate\nany architectural effect or false blocking dependency.\n\nThis is one pipeline-con\n…[15118 of 18190 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:985afd07fc45be7d]…\nl/scalar_lanes.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Add the combinational scalar execution lanes, driven by registered operation enables rather than a live encoded opcode. Implement exact RV32I arithmetic, Boolean, comparison, independent left shift, signed shared right shift, LUI and link results with a balanced one-hot result merge and no extra clock.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_scalar_lanes.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare every lane against independent RV32I integer expectations, including random operands, carry/borrow/sign extrema, every shift count and upper shift-count bits. Check mutually exclusive lane controls and exact operation mapping.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Keep all existing assertions and add scalar forwarding/source-selection streams covering both sources, PC/immediate versus register operands, competing writers, held-WB refresh, load-use, both bus stalls, reset and wrong-path squashes. Require unchanged retirement spacing and correct RVFI operands.\"\n  }\n]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
