{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_30", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261001-003-r10s2','hyp-20261001-001-r9s0','hyp-20261001-002-r13s1']:\n  print(r['id'])\n  h=r['hypothesis']; print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('ERROR',r.get('error'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-001-r9s0\nChange only the representation and consumption of registered operand\nforwarding choices. Keep forward_unit's current two-bit lookahead\noutputs and its EX-over-MEM-over-RF priority. In id_stage, convert each\naccepted lookahead choice into a registered three-bit one-hot selector:\nRF/captured operand=001, EX/MEM scalar result=010, MEM/WB result=100.\nReset both selectors to 001. Move this conversion into the existing\nID/EX acceptance edge so EX receives already decoded selection bits.\n\nRewrite EX's two forwarding case muxes as masked ORs:\nrs1 = (mask(sel1[0]) & in.rs1_val) |\n      (mask(sel1[1]) & fwd_ex_mem) |\n      (mask(sel1[2]) & fwd_mem_wb);\nrs2 uses the identical expression for source 2.\nmask replicates one bit 32 times. Exactly one select is set, so the\nexpression is bit-for-bit equivalent to the current mux. This removes\nbinary selector decoding from the late WB-data-to-comparison path\nand gives synthesis a flat three-source combinational network.\n\nUpdate all held-selector transitions consistently. When a held EX\ninstruction sees MEM advance, select 100 only for the matching MEM\nwriter and 001 otherwise. When MEM is held, preserve 010 even if an\nolder WB write refreshes the stored operand. For a WB refresh with\nany other selection, switch to 001. Preserve every existing operand\nrefresh, x0 rule, actual producer qualification and load-use hold.\nBoth selectors must remain one-hot through reset, flush, bubbles,\nmemory s