{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\"|\\\"category\\\":\\\"structural\\\"|multipl|pipeline|timing|worst' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Shared radix-4 combinational divider with borrow-based digit selection\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz, with a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst\\npath crossing operand forwarding and the combinational ALU. The four\\nsigned/unsigned division and remainder expressions in alu.sv are the\\nstrongest candidate for this deep arithmetic path. CoreMark fitness\\nscales directly with Fmax when instruction latency and cycle count stay\\nconstant. There are no earlier bench hypotheses or recorded lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz, with a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst\\npath crossing operand forwarding and the combinational ALU. The four\\nsigned/unsigned division and remainder expressions in alu.sv are the\\nstrongest candidate for this deep arithmetic path. CoreMark fitness\\nscales directly with Fmax when instruction latency and cycle count stay\\nconstant. There are no earlier bench hypotheses or recorded lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one shared, fully\\ncombinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divider. Convert operands to\\nunsigned magnitudes for DIV and REM, and use the original bit patterns\\nfor DIVU and REMU. Precompute widened divisor multiples B, 2B and 3B.\\nUnroll 16 digit stages, consuming the dividend from its most significant\\npair of bits to its least significant pair. At each stage form the\\nwidened partial dividend P = 4*remainder + next_pair, calculate P-B,\\nP-2B and P-3B in parallel, and select the largest nonnegative trial to\\nemit quotient digit 0, 1, 2 or 3 and the corresponding new remainder.\\nDerive trial validity from each widened subtraction's borrow bit rather\\nthan instantiating a separate magnitude comparator followed by another\\nsubtraction. Use sufficient unsigned width throughout: divisor\\nmultiples and partial dividends require 34 bits, and trial differences\\nrequire 35 bits to retain underflow. Expose quotient and remainder fr\n…[88330 of 91402 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ef98743c89f1e5e6]…\ness\": 112.68, \"delta_pct\": 6.93, \"vs_baseline\": 829.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 47.218, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4190281, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3392, \"ff\": 780, \"seeds\": [45.508, 47.218, 47.218], \"perturbations\": [[0, 45.508, 17], [1, 47.218, 16], [2, 47.218, 16]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.974, \"arrival_ns\": 27.269, \"logic_cells\": 17, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 17, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T02:44:18.873999Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 (improvement, +6.93%): Pairing a 64-entry BHT/JAL predictor with validity-only ID/EX recovery removes correct-prediction flush bubbles without routing EX redirects through instruction masking or wide payload enables, making prediction profitable on the five-step divider.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
