{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n e=json.loads(line)\n print(e['id'],e['category'],e.get('outcome'),e.get('fitness'),e.get('fmax_mhz'),e.get('cycles'))\n if e['category']=='structural':\n  h=e.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('CRITICAL:',e.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-4a6c0e6 micro_opt improvement 12.12 5.442 4491485\nhyp-20261001-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression 13.98 6.277 4491485\nhyp-20261001-002-r1s1 structural improvement 68.17 30.617 4491485\nKeep the existing single-issue pipeline and combinational RV32I/MUL\ndatapaths, but execute DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU in a separate registered\ndivider that performs eight radix-2 restoring steps per clock and\ncompletes its 32 quotient bits in four clocks. Remove all / and % operators\nfrom the ordinary ALU. Capture the forwarded operands and instruction\nmetadata once, then use a shared unsigned quotient/remainder engine\nwith at most eight serial 33-bit trial subtract/select updates per\ncycle, rather than the baseline's full 32-step combinational divide.\nUse separate registered magnitude preparation and final sign\ncorrection; no cycle combines those with the quotient loop. Return a\nresult within six clocks after accepting operands: one magnitude\npreparation clock, four quotient clocks and one correction clock.\nHandle divide-by-zero and signed overflow explicitly. MUL, MULH,\nMULHU and MULHSU remain unchanged. This is one divider-topology change;\nretain the rest of the pipeline and avoid unrelated throughput work.\n\nA valid division occupies EX until its result is available. Freeze\nfetch/decode and prevent younger instructions from entering EX; older\ninstructions continue through MEM/WB. Once the previous EX/MEM entry\nis accepted by MEM, replace it with an invalid entry while the divider\nruns rather than repeatedly retiring it. A stalled older data-memory\nrequest keeps its EX/MEM payload and bus outputs stable. Latch the\ndivider's result and all RVFI metadata until EX/MEM can accept them,\nthen enqueue the instruction exactly once. Capture operands only on\na single accepted start event, using existing forwarding, and preserve\nheld ID/EX source values when their producers drain from MEM/WB.\nRegister-file writes, redirects and memory enables require valid\ninstructions; divider backpressure must not suppress older commits\nor replay a \n…[14148 of 17220 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:09846fcbeff18b95]…\nlled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker-window gates.\n\nExpected improvement is 18 percent, with medium confidence. The gain\nmust come from a genuine shorter M arithmetic topology, and must exceed\nmultiplication's additional CoreMark cycles. At unchanged marker cycles\nthe 4.6 percent acceptance bar requires approximately 49.39 MHz; if\ncycles increase by 10 percent it requires approximately 54.33 MHz.\nMeasure actual cycles and all three vendor placement options. The main\nrisks are multiplication frequency in the matrix kernel, launch-edge\nmagnitude/seed delay, product-reduction delay, and another ordinary\nforwarding or branch path becoming critical. No timing or correctness\ngain for the proposed circuit has yet been measured.\n\nCRITICAL: {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_m/u_div/remainder_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -14.174, 'arrival_ns': 24.469, 'logic_cells': 25, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_m/u_div']}\nhyp-20261001-003-r4s2 predictor regression 112.78 47.259 4190281\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
