{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r5s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace('terms and a balanced residual mux. Append that three-bit digit to', '''terms and a balanced residual mux. With fit[k]=no_borrow(T-kD),\nuse select[0]=\"'!fit[1], select[k]=fit[k]&&!fit[k+1] for k=1..6,\nand select[7]=fit[7]. OR the mutually exclusive masked residuals\nand encode the selected digit without a serial priority chain.\nAppend that three-bit digit to'\"''')\na=h['hypothesis'].index('Expected fitness gain is 12 percent')\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'][:a]+'''An isolated scratch prototype of exactly this two-group topology,\nwith all other champion RTL unchanged, passed the six existing\nreal/ALTOPS divider, shared M-unit and core dependency test\nconfigurations. Those suites verify exact arithmetic, changing inputs\nwhile busy, reset in every execution phase, held completion, memory\nstalls, mixed operation dependencies and the ten-clock ready-bus\ncontrol-transfer-to-DIV retirement ceiling. Gowin placement options\n0/1/2 measured 60.117/61.075/61.075 MHz, median 61.075 MHz, with\n4111 logic cells and 1114 registers versus champion 3616/982. The\nnew worst paths are ordinary forwarding/ALU and branch-training paths,\nnot the divider launch or recurrence. The unchanged canonical -O3\n2K/10-iteration CoreMark binary under both bus stalls passed all five\nexpected CRCs, UART validation and bounds checks, with markers at\ncycles 15235 and 4393389: exactly 4378154 measured cycles, matching\nthe champion. Computed prototype fitness is 139.499 iterations/second,\n11.796 percent above 124.78, exceeding the 4.6 percent acceptance bar.\nThis is proposal-stage evidence; require a fresh unmodified evaluator\nrun after implementation rather than treating it as acceptance.\n\nExpected fitness gain is 12 percent with medium confidence. At unchanged\nmarker cycles acceptance requires median Fmax above 57.143 MHz. The\nremaining risks are implementation differences in trial selection or\nregister preservation and PREP magnitude/multiple routing. Retain\nall original correctness gates and require the full unchanged formal\nsuite as well as real arithmetic and vendor timing checks. A full\nscratch copy of the existing ALTOPS formal suite is currently running;\nno contract or shared riscv-formal files were changed.\n'''\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef multiline(dumper, value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nD.add_representer(str,multiline)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=85))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote measured proposal-stage evidence; schema valid')\nlogs=list(Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/bf842e9a/b4edfa90/radix32_probe/formal/riscv-formal/cores').glob('bench-*/checks/*/logfile.txt'))\npassed=[q.parent.name for q in logs if 'DONE (PASS' in q.read_text()]\nfailed=[q.parent.name for q in logs if 'DONE (FAIL' in q.read_text() or 'DONE (ERROR' in q.read_text()]\nrunning=[q.parent.name for q in logs if q.parent.name not in passed+failed]\nprint('Formal status:', len(passed),'passed;', failed,'failed;',running,'pending')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
