{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 (improvement, +462.46%): Replacing ALU `/` and `%` with four registered groups of eight restoring steps and separate magnitude/sign stages shortens the critical path enough to outweigh six-cycle DIV/REM latency in CoreMark's division-light timed kernels.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 (regression, +11.47%): A 64-entry folded-PC BHT plus direct JAL prediction raised CoreMark throughput 7.19% by avoiding EX flush bubbles, but the forwarded combinational DIV/REM path still limited Fmax to 5.66 MHz, making divider pipelining the higher-impact change.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r2s1 (improvement, +54.58%): Reducing div_unit's serial restoring steps per register from eight to five improves timing without increasing CoreMark's marker cycles, while folding magnitude/sign work into launch/accept edges preserves the ten-clock branch-to-DIV liveness bound despite seven LOOP clocks.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r2s2 (regression, +11.18%): A 64-entry BHT/JAL predictor with one-bit direction recovery removes CoreMark flush bubbles while retaining divider-limited timing, but eight serial restoring steps per divider clock leave Fmax at 31.76 MHz versus the five-step divider's 47.33 MHz.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 (improvement, +6.93%): Pairing a 64-entry BHT/JAL predictor with validity-only ID/EX recovery removes correct-prediction flush bubbles without routing EX redirects through instruction masking or wide payload enables, making prediction profitable on the five-step divider.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r4s1 (improvement, +10.74%): With MUL and DIV tied for the critical path, registering MUL limb products and carry-save reduction while seeding four DIV bits at launch shortens both arithmetic cones enough to offset CoreMark's two extra MUL clocks without lengthening the seven-loop divider schedule.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r5s1 (improvement, +8.11%): Consuming five quotient bits per LOOP with parallel radix-8/radix-4 trials frees a PREP clock for preserved raw-operand \n…[1393 of 4465 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:35adbc8e188c5429]…\nnLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
