{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261001-002-r6s1|hyp-20261001-001-r6s0|hyp-20261001-003-r6s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Partition DIV and REM across four registered arithmetic steps\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 at only 5.442 MHz. Its worst reported path\\npasses through forwarding and u_ex/u_alu, with 156 cells and 199.837 ns\\narrival time. The current ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder as combinational / and % expressions. Those operators\\ncreate long arithmetic chains that constrain the clock for every\\ninstruction. There are no previous structural attempts in the target's\\nhistory and no LESSONS.md. Replacing this execution topology is a more\\npromising structural change than increasing instruction throughput\\nwhile retaining the same slow combinational datapath.\\nSource inspection shows that the timed list, matrix and state kernels\\nemphasize pointer operations, multiplication and CRC/bit operations;\\nsource-level divisions occur mainly in initialization and reporting.\\nThis makes extra DIV/REM latency a promising trade for higher Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline scores 12.12 at only 5.442 MHz. Its worst reported path\\npasses through forwarding and u_ex/u_alu, with 156 cells and 199.837 ns\\narrival time. The current ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder as combinational / and % expressions. Those operators\\ncreate long arithmetic chains that constrain the clock for every\\ninstruction. There are no previous structural attempts in the target's\\nhistory and no LESSONS.md. Replacing this execution topology is a more\\npromising structural change than increasing instruction throughput\\nwhile retaining the same slow combinational datapath.\\nSource inspection shows that the timed list, matrix and state kernels\\nemphasize pointer operations, multiplication and CRC/bit operations;\\nsource-level divisions occur mainly in initialization and reporting.\\nThis makes extra DIV/REM latency a promising trade for higher Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the existing single-issue pipeline and combinationa\n…[84094 of 87166 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8bef5fd82f7de018]…\nvs_baseline\": 1027.15, \"fmax_mhz\": 59.809, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4378154, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4053, \"ff\": 1147, \"seeds\": [55.631, 59.809, 59.809], \"perturbations\": [[0, 55.631, 18], [1, 59.809, 17], [2, 59.809, 17]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_addr_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -12.976, \"arrival_ns\": 23.27, \"logic_cells\": 23, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 18, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T04:45:29.244058Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r6s2 (regression, +1.27%): Replacing the BHT's variable-index read-modify-write with bank/row-enabled local Boolean counter feedback preserves prediction behavior, so with the champion's critical path outside the predictor this topology cleanup offers no cycle savings and falls short of the 4.6% fitness threshold.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
