{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'], d['category'], d['title'])\n print('RESULT',d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'),d.get('critical_path'))\n if d['category']=='structural' or any(s in d['title'].lower() for s in ['successor','recovery','branch']):\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print('PROPOSAL',h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-4a6c0e6 micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench\nRESULT improvement 12.12 5.442 4491485 {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261001-001-r1s0 micro_opt Shared radix-4 combinational divider with borrow-based digit selection\nRESULT regression 13.98 6.277 4491485 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -156.85, 'arrival_ns': 167.145, 'logic_cells': 452, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261001-002-r1s1 structural Partition DIV and REM across four registered arithmetic steps\nRESULT improvement 68.17 30.617 4491485 {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_10_s0', 'slack_ns': -28.061, 'arrival_ns': 38.355, 'logic_cells': 252, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\nPROPOSAL Keep the existing single-issue pipeline and combinational RV32I/MUL\ndatapaths, but execute DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU in a separate registered\ndivider that performs eight radix-2 restoring steps per clock and\ncompletes its 32 quotient bits in four clocks. Remove all / and % operators\nfrom the ordinary ALU. Capture the forwarded operands and instruction\nmetadata once, then use a shared unsigned quotient/remainder engine\nwith at most eight serial 33-bit trial subtract/select updates per\ncycle, rather than the baseline's full 32-step combinational divide.\nUse separate registered magnitude preparation and final sign\ncorrection; no cycle combines those with the quotient loop. Return a\nresult within six clocks after accepting operands: one magnitude\npreparation clock, four quotient clocks and one correction clock.\nHandle divide-by-zero and signed overflow explicitly. MUL, MULH,\nMULHU and MULHSU remain unchanged. This is one divider-topology change;\nretain the rest of the pipeline and avoid unrelated throughput work.\n\nA valid division \n…[35955 of 39027 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7aa1074e75f6956c]…\na, and requests held under independent bus stalls. Check that\nflushes, reset and M drain bubbles issue no accesses and that accepted\nstores and retirements occur exactly once. Retain all original tests\nand formal assertions, including the ten-clock progress bound. Require\nfull-trace cosim and canonical 2K/10-iteration CoreMark CRCs, UART,\nbounds and marker-window validation. Evaluate the median across all\nthree Gowin placement options. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires\nFmax above 61.778 MHz. Expected fitness gain is 12 percent; remaining\nrisks are the new EX mask/address cone and a forwarding or predictor\npath becoming the next limit. Fresh evaluator results remain required.\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r6s2 predictor Locally updated banked flop BHT without a training read mux\nRESULT regression 136.61 59.809 4378154 {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_addr_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -12.976, 'arrival_ns': 23.27, 'logic_cells': 23, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
