data bits, and decode\n  the write bank and row outside each word's data feedback. Keep the\n  two read ports independent. Use Gowin-supported register preservation\n  and non-RAM coding where needed; verify that the mapped RF uses\n  flip-flops rather than BSRAM or inferred RAM wi\n…[3385 of 6457 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bcc4773640cb797a]…\nboundary in the vendor netlist.\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all existing assertions and add full-register populated\n      reset, bank/row boundaries, independent dual reads, both-port\n      write-first collisions, x0 collisions and randomized read/write\n      sequences checked against an architectural register-file model.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain current timing and predictor assertions. Check two-source\n      forwarding and WB/read collisions into ALU, branch/JALR and memory\n      operations across banks, including long dmem holds and exact raw\n      RVFI operand values, PC continuity and no wrong-path effects.\n  - file: test/test_core_div.py\n    description: |\n      Keep every real/ALTOPS arithmetic and ten-clock progress check.\n      Extend operand refresh and dependencies across RF banks while\n      older writers drain during memory/M holds, with reset cancellation\n      and exact-once acceptance/retirement at the existing latency.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
