er expressions in alu.sv are the\\nstrongest candidate for this deep arithmetic path. CoreMark fitness\\nscales directly with Fmax when instruction latency and cycle count stay\\nconstant. There are no earlier bench hypotheses or recorded lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one shared, fully\\ncombinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divider. Convert operands to\\nunsigned magn\n…[17463 of 20535 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8228d921c070c9a1]…\nutcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 68.17, \"delta_pct\": 462.46, \"vs_baseline\": 462.46, \"fmax_mhz\": 30.617, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3010, \"ff\": 712, \"seeds\": [30.247, 30.617, 30.617], \"perturbations\": [[0, 30.247, 48], [1, 30.617, 48], [2, 30.617, 48]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_10_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -28.061, \"arrival_ns\": 38.355, \"logic_cells\": 252, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 48, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T01:42:44.889193Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 (improvement, +462.46%): Replacing ALU `/` and `%` with four registered groups of eight restoring steps and separate magnitude/sign stages shortens the critical path enough to outweigh six-cycle DIV/REM latency in CoreMark's division-light timed kernels.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
