{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id')=='hyp-20261001-002-r7s1':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Rebuild operand delivery around the existing ID/EX acceptance edge:\nuse fixed-word flop RF storage and register the forwarding selections\none cycle ahead in decode. EX consumes registered source choices\ninstead of comparing live producer tags before its operand muxes.\nThis is a single structural repartition of register reads and bypass\ncontrol, with the existing pipeline depth and instruction schedule.\n\nImplement x1-x31 as fixed-address generated 32-bit flop words,\narranged in four banks of eight logical entries. x0 has no storage.\nDecode write bank/row into local word enables; synchronous reset\nclears all architectural values. For each independent asynchronous\nread port, share row/bank address decode across the data bits and\nform balanced masked-OR reductions within and between banks.\nPreserve both same-cycle valid nonzero WB-to-read bypasses. Do not\ninfer RAM or change reset semantics. Make the existing two ID/EX\noperand registers explicit preserved flops, with unchanged capture,\nreset, validity-only squash and held-WB-refresh transitions. Verify\nthat Gowin removes the two RF BSRAMs and retains operand storage.\n\nMove dependency comparison and youngest-producer priority from EX\nto decode. For each raw fetched source, compute the selector that\nwill be correct after the next ID/EX edge: 00 uses the captured RF\nvalue; 01 uses the advancing current EX instruction's next EX/MEM\nscalar result; 10 uses the current EX/MEM instruction's next MEM/WB\nresult, including loaded data. The current EX producer has priority\nover current MEM, and x0 is never a producer. Capture both two