{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\"|r10s2|r11s2|return.address|gshare|local history|indirect|RAS' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"64-entry folded-PC bimodal prediction at fetch\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline has no branch prediction: every aligned taken conditional\\nbranch and every JAL/JALR redirects in EX and discards the current fetch.\\nIF/ID is combinational, so a correctly predicted direct transfer can\\neliminate the one-cycle recovery bubble without adding a pipeline stage.\\nCoreMark repeatedly executes loops and direct calls, making a small\\nadaptive direction predictor a promising way to increase iterations/cycle.\\nProfiling the canonical 2K, -O3, 10-iteration instruction stream between\\nits MMIO markers finds 529588 conditional branches, of which 294425 are\\ntaken, plus 49367 direct JALs. A 64-entry table with a folded PC index\\npredicts about 92.2 percent of conditional branches correctly.\\nThe measured critical path is the forwarded combinational M-extension\\nALU, not branch lookup; this proposal targets throughput while keeping\\npredictor storage and added fetch logic small enough to preserve Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline has no branch prediction: every aligned taken conditional\\nbranch and every JAL/JALR redirects in EX and discards the current fetch.\\nIF/ID is combinational, so a correctly predicted direct transfer can\\neliminate the one-cycle recovery bubble without adding a pipeline stage.\\nCoreMark repeatedly executes loops and direct calls, making a small\\nadaptive direction predictor a promising way to increase iterations/cycle.\\nProfiling the canonical 2K, -O3, 10-iteration instruction stream between\\nits MMIO markers finds 529588 conditional branches, of which 294425 are\\ntaken, plus 49367 direct JALs. A 64-entry table with a folded PC index\\npredicts about 92.2 percent of conditional branches correctly.\\nThe measured critical path is the forwarded combinational M-extension\\nALU, not branch lookup; this proposal targets throughput while keeping\\npredictor storage and added fetch logic small enough to preserve Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\n…[141232 of 144304 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c19c2a603b293cca]…\nhe mask holds\\nwith its payload through load-use, data and M holds. Compare table\\nupdates and fetch predictions against the unchanged independent\\nmodel, including back-to-back branches, folded aliases, invalid\\nraw masks after recovery, imem stalls and reset.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 177.04, \"delta_pct\": -3.11, \"vs_baseline\": 1360.73, \"fmax_mhz\": 77.511, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4378154, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6541, \"ff\": 2234, \"seeds\": [75.3, 77.511, 77.511], \"perturbations\": [[0, 75.3, 15], [1, 77.511, 12], [2, 77.511, 12]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.mem_to_reg_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_30_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -8.28, \"arrival_ns\": 18.575, \"logic_cells\": 29, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_rf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T08:24:48.009448Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
