{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20261001-003-r9s2','hyp-20261001-003-r5s2','hyp-20261001-003-r6s2'):\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(r['id'])\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r5s2\nPreserve the successful 64x2-bit folded-PC bimodal predictor, but replace\nits reset-all counter implementation with FPGA distributed LUT RAM and\none serialized cold-initialization controller. This is one predictor\nstorage change; retain the current raw legal-branch/JAL predecode,\ndirect-target arithmetic, speculation bounds and alignment checks,\npredicted_taken metadata, direct one-bit EX verification, validity-only\nrecovery and sequential JALR policy.\n\nRemove reset assignment from the counter array. Reset only a seven-bit\ninitialization count to zero. On each non-reset edge while count[6] is\nzero, write 2'b01 to counters[count[5:0]] and increment the count. The\nedge that writes entry 63 changes the count to 64; then hold it at 64\nuntil reset. Predict conditional branches sequentially during these\n64 cold-start clocks, and discard conditional-branch training during\ninitialization because the single RAM write port belongs to the sweep.\nDirect JAL prediction remains active throughout initialization. The\nsweep must run independently of fetch stalls, dmem stalls and M holds;\nit must never stall the CPU or alter architectural next-PC resolution.\nReset restarts the entire sweep, including if it interrupts a sweep.\n\nAfter initialization, use the exact current index PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]\nfor both lookup and training, the same weakly-not-taken state, and\nold-counter simultaneous read/write semantics. Fetch needs the direction\nMSB at fetch_index; training reads the complete old counter at train_index.\nInfer asynchronous distributed RAM with one clocked write port; Gowin\nmay replicate the small RAM to provide the two independent read ports.\nUse portable inference and a distributed-RAM synthesis hint rather than\ninstantiating vendor primitives that cannot run through Verilator and\nriscv-formal. No unknown RAM bit may affect prediction before all entries\nare initialized, including repeated or partial resets.\n\nExpress the training transition with two small Boolean functions and\nwrite on every qualified tra\n…[8222 of 11294 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9fb0b3bd47af9aa3]…\nclock progress bounds, formal/cosim gates,\ncanonical CRC/UART/bounds/markers and exactly 4378154 CoreMark cycles.\n\nAn isolated compact three-plane prototype using COMBINATIONAL plane\nmasks measured 72.427/77.878/77.878 MHz across Gowin options 0/1/2:\nmedian 77.878 MHz, 6599 logic cells and 2170 registers. That is only a\n1.85 percent frequency gain and does not pass acceptance. This proposal\nspecifically adds the decode-registered one-hot mask to remove its\nremaining encoded-selector decode and plane-arbitration control cone.\nThat final refinement has not been timed; confidence is low. A broader\nnine-source-pair prototype passed all 31 current pipeline tests but\nregressed timing, supporting the compact scope rather than replication\nacross every source pair. Require fresh correctness gates and all three\nvendor placements for the final implementation. At unchanged cycles,\nacceptance needs median Fmax above 79.983436 MHz and fitness above\n182.6839 iterations/second; ALU or divider recurrence can still limit it.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
