{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nkeys=('target arithmetic','target formation','narrow','carry-select','gshare','perfect','1.3 percent','return stack','BTB')\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x.get('category')=='predictor' and any(k.lower() in str(x).lower() for k in keys):\n  print(x['id'],x['title'])\n  h=x.get('hypothesis',{}); s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n  for p in s.split('\\\\n\\\\n'):\n   if any(k.lower() in p.lower() for k in keys) and not p.startswith('Preserve'): print(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 64-entry folded-PC bimodal prediction at fetch\nAdd a 64-entry PC-indexed bimodal table of two-bit saturating counters,\ninitialized to weakly not taken (01). Index it with the six-bit XOR\nfetch PC[7:2] ^ fetch PC[13:8], use\nthe counter MSB for legal conditional branches, and compute their B-type\ntarget directly from the fetched instruction. Predict legal aligned JAL\nunconditionally taken using its J-type immediate. Leave JALR predicted\nsequential and resolve it in EX. This is one direct-control-flow predictor;\nno BTB, global history, return stack, or instruction buffering is needed.\nhyp-20261001-003-r2s2 Compact bimodal direct-transfer prediction on the registered-divider champion\nAdd one small direct-control-flow predictor: a 64-entry table of two-bit\nsaturating direction counters, indexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], together\nwith unconditional direct JAL prediction. Initialize counters to weakly\nnot taken (01). Use their MSB only for legal conditional branch encodings\n(opcode 0x63 and funct3 in {0,1,4,5,6,7}). Predecode raw imem_data, form\nthe B/J immediate and PC-relative target, and select that target only\nwhen predicted taken, word aligned, and within instruction memory\n[0x00000000,0x00100000). Otherwise predict PC+4. Leave JALR sequential\nfor architectural resolution in EX. Do not add a BTB, global history,\nreturn stack, instruction buffer, or pipeline stage.\nhyp-20261001-003-r4s2 Carry fetch-computed successors into predictor verification\nIn EX, reuse the captured direct target for legal conditional branches\nand JAL, and the sequential successor for fallthrough, jump link data,\ntrap fallback and divider metadata. Keep the forwarded rs1+immediate\nJALR calculation and its bit-zero clearing unchanged. Use the raw\ncaptured direct target for branch/JAL misalignment checks. Preserve\nactual_transfer XOR predicted_taken recovery, once-per-advance legal\nconditional training and architectural RVFI pc_wdata. Do not carry a\nredundant predicted-next-PC comparator or introduce a BTB or history\npredictor. The accepted instruction fixes its B/J target, so the\nexisting one-bit direction check remains sufficient.\nhyp-20261001-003-r5s2 LUT-RAM bimodal predictor with serialized cold initialization\nhyp-20261001-003-r7s2 Split normal and recovery fetch-address registers\nhyp-20261001-003-r8s2 Direction-specific predictor recovery rails into one fetch PC\nThe tested prequalifiers are precisely:\nD = !dec_is_illegal && !in.predicted_taken &&\n    (dec_is_branch || (dec_is_jump && !dec_is_jalr)) &&\n    ((in.pc[1:0] + imm[1:0]) modulo 4 == 0);\nF = !dec_is_illegal && dec_is_branch && in.predicted_taken;\nR = !dec_is_illegal && dec_is_jalr.\nRegister these on the existing ID payload capture. With\nA = in.valid && !reset && !stall && !m_busy in EX, the rails are\nt = A && D && (in.ctrl.is_jump || branch_cond),\nf = A && F && !branch_cond, and\nr = A && R && !jalr_sum[1].\nF relies on the existing effective predicted_taken guarantee that the\naccepted direct target was aligned and bounded; never substitute the\nraw BHT direction bit. JALR bit zero is ignored architecturally, while\nbit one must be zero. The three candidate values are branch_target\n(the same PC+imm for both branch and JAL), in.pc+4, and\n{jalr_sum[31:1],1'b0}, respectively. No target is narrowed to RAM width.\nhyp-20261001-003-r9s2 Decode-selected branch predicate forwarding for predictor recovery\nhyp-20261001-003-r10s2 Predict through load-dependent branches and verify them in MEM\nhyp-20261001-003-r11s2 Decode-preselected local feedback for bimodal predictor training\nhyp-20261001-003-r12s2 Decode-prepared BHT transitions with outcome-only training selection\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
