{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x['id'] in ('hyp-20261001-003-r9s2','hyp-20261001-003-r10s2','hyp-20261001-002-r12s1'):\n  print(x['id'], x['title'])\n  h=x.get('hypothesis',{}); print(h.get('motivation','') if isinstance(h,dict) else '')\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r9s2 Decode-selected branch predicate forwarding for predictor recovery\nThe champion scores 174.65 at 76.466 MHz with 4378154 CoreMark marker\ncycles. Prior history limits additional prediction-accuracy benefit to\napproximately 1.3 percent, below the acceptance margin. Its option-0\nworst path actually ends at a BHT counter clock enable: MEM/WB load\ndata crosses WB operand selection, EX comparison and high-fanout\npredictor training logic. The same late comparison controls fetch\nrecovery. Earlier comparator sharing retained the scalar operand mux\nbefore comparison, while predictor counter and recovery-PC changes\ndid not clear the bar. Forwarding compact comparison predicates offers\na different way to shorten this late predictor feedback path.\n\nKeep the BHT, direct JAL prediction, one-bit accepted direction,\nregistered recovery predicates and same-cycle EX correction schedule.\nChange the predictor's branch-verification operand topology: compare\nthe late WB value before selecting the branch predicate, rather than\nselecting two 32-bit forwarded operands before comparing them.\n\nForm early_a = fwd_rs1_sel == 1 ? fwd_ex_mem : in.rs1_val and\nearly_b = fwd_rs2_sel == 1 ? fwd_ex_mem : in.rs2_val. These select only\nregistered ID/EX and EX/MEM sources. Construct three parallel comparison\nplanes for (early_a, early_b), (early_a, fwd_mem_wb), and\n(fwd_mem_wb, early_b). The fourth plane, where both operands select the\nsame WB value, is constant: equality true and both less-than relations\nfalse. Each nonconstant plane produces equality, unsigned less-than\nand signed less-than; share its unsigned comparison with signed sign\ncorrection: signed_lt = signs_differ ? lhs[31] : unsigned_lt.\nThis keeps late WB data out of the existing wide operand mux on its\nroute into branch verification. Scalar ALU, JALR, memory and M-unit\noperands continue to use the existing forwarding datapath.\n\nRegister the four mutually exclusive plane-selection bits at the ID/EX\nboundary, alongside the existing maintained forwarding selectors.\nCom\n…[17308 of 20380 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f535e3f7515fe7c9]…\ned RVFI retirement.\nWrong-path entries must never retire, train, issue memory or launch M.\nPreserve real/ALTOPS arithmetic and the unchanged ten-clock formal\nliveness bounds; empty bypass and immediate corrected fetch acceptance\nadd no ready-bus recovery stage.\n\nRequire independent FIFO token conservation, effective-PC transitions\nand delayed-training references. Cover empty/full, pointer wraparound,\nall push/pop combinations, stable blocked heads, buffered issue during\nimem stalls, long data/M holds, recovery of a full queue, blocked\ncorrected fetches, both branch correction directions, forwarded JALR\nand reset. Adapt old physical-fetch-equals-decode assumptions without\nweakening architectural assertions. Require the unchanged formal,\ncosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds and median vendor timing\ngates. Divider recurrence and the queued-head-to-RF path now limit the\nprototype, so acceptance comes from hiding fetch stalls at approximately\nunchanged Fmax, not from claiming a large clock-rate improvement.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport random\nmask=(1<<32)-1\n\ndef sext(x,n): return x-(1<<n) if x>>(n-1) else x\n\ndef bounded(pc,imm):\n s=int(imm<0)\n a,b=pc&0xfffff,imm&0xfffff\n lo=(a&1023)+(b&1023)\n hi0=(a>>10)+(b>>10)\n hi=hi0+int(lo>1023)\n c=int(hi>1023)\n target=((hi&1023)<<10)|(lo&1023)\n u=pc>>20\n inrange=(u==0 and c==s) or (u==1 and s==1 and c==0) or (u==4095 and s==0 and c==1)\n return inrange,target\nrng=random.Random(0x13_2)\npcs=(0,1,2,3,0x3fc,0x3fe,0x3ff,0x400,0xff800,0xffff8,0xffffc,0xfffff,0x100000,0x100004,0x1fffff,0xfff00000,0xfffffff8,0xfffffffc,0xffffffff)\nimm12=(-4096,-4094,-2048,-1026,-1024,-1022,-4,-2,0,2,4,1022,1024,1026,2046,4092,4094)\nimm20=(-1048576,-1048574,-524288,-4096,-1024,-4,-2,0,2,4,1022,1024,4094,524286,1048572,1048574)\nchecked=0\nfor n,offsets in ((13,imm12),(21,imm20)):\n for pc in pcs:\n  for imm in offsets:\n   ok,target=bounded(pc,imm)\n   exact=(pc+imm)&mask\n   assert ok==(exact<1<<20), (pc,imm,ok,exact)\n   assert not ok or target==exact, (pc,imm,target,exact)\n   checked+=1\n for _ in range(200000):\n  pc=rng.getrandbits(32) if rng.randrange(4)==0 else rng.choice((0,0x100000,0xfff00000))|rng.getrandbits(20)\n  imm=sext(rng.getrandbits(n)&~1,n)\n  ok,target=bounded(pc,imm)\n  exact=(pc+imm)&mask\n  assert ok==(exact<1<<20)\n  assert not ok or target==exact\n  checked+=1\nprint('Independent modulo-32-bit reference matched',checked,'target cases; both B/J widths, carry-select and bounds.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
