{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(r['id'],r['title'],r.get('outcome'),r.get('fitness'),r.get('cycles'),r.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{}); h=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n  if any(x in h.lower() for x in ('return stack','local history','gshare','target cache','btb','return-address')):\n   print(h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 64-entry folded-PC bimodal prediction at fetch regression 13.51 4190307 5.66\nAdd a 64-entry PC-indexed bimodal table of two-bit saturating counters,\ninitialized to weakly not taken (01). Index it with the six-bit XOR\nfetch PC[7:2] ^ fetch PC[13:8], use\nthe counter MSB for legal conditional branches, and compute their B-type\ntarget directly from the fetched instruction. Predict legal aligned JAL\nunconditionally taken using its J-type immediate. Leave JALR predicted\nsequential and resolve it in EX. This is one direct-control-flow predictor;\nno BTB, global history, return stack, or instruction buffering is needed.\n\nBecause this core exposes imem_data combinationally in IF, the predicted\nnext PC can be installed at the same edge that accepts the instruction\ninto ID/EX. Add predicted_next_pc to IF/ID and ID/EX, and capture it with\nexactly the same enable as the instruction. Compute prediction from raw\nimem_data and PC rather than the flush-masked instruction bundle, avoiding\ncombinational feedback through the hazard unit. Restrict early branch\nclassification to opcode 0x63 with funct3 in {0,1,4,5,6,7}; JAL uses 0x6f.\nPredict sequential whenever the proposed direct target is misaligned\nor outside instruction memory [0x00000000, 0x00100000). The bounds gate\napplies only to speculation and preserves architectural EX resolution.\n\nIn EX, retain the existing forwarding, branch comparison, JAL/JALR link\nresult, and trap handling. Form the architectural resolved next PC using\nthe existing semantics, including pc+4 on a misalignment trap. Redirect\nand squash the younger fetched instruction only when this resolved PC\ndiffers from the accepted predicted_next_pc. Both taken-to-not-taken and\nnot-taken-to-taken errors must recover, as must a wrong target. Keep RVFI\npc_wdata equal to the resolved architectural PC, never the prediction.\n\nOnly a valid EX instruction that advances to EX/MEM may issue recovery\nor update the predictor: gate both with !stall_ex_mem. Train only legal,\nnon-trapping conditional branches\n…[8530 of 11602 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b1e73fe5754ab1a9]…\n-r5s2 LUT-RAM bimodal predictor with serialized cold initialization regression 121.01 4378154 52.98\nhyp-20261001-003-r6s2 Locally updated banked flop BHT without a training read mux regression 136.61 4378154 59.809\nhyp-20261001-003-r7s2 Split normal and recovery fetch-address registers regression 135.54 4378154 59.343\nhyp-20261001-003-r8s2 Direction-specific predictor recovery rails into one fetch PC regression 171.85 4378154 75.24\nhyp-20261001-003-r9s2 Decode-selected branch predicate forwarding for predictor recovery regression 165.29 4378154 72.366\nhyp-20261001-003-r10s2 Predict through load-dependent branches and verify them in MEM broken None None None\nhyp-20261001-003-r11s2 Decode-preselected local feedback for bimodal predictor training regression 177.04 4378154 77.511\nhyp-20261001-003-r12s2 Decode-prepared BHT transitions with outcome-only training selection regression 176.94 4378154 77.469\nhyp-20261001-003-r13s2 Parallel bounded target arithmetic for fetch prediction regression 199.24 4095164 81.594\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
