{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20261001-002-r12s1','hyp-20261001-003-r12s2','hyp-20261001-003-r11s2'):\n  print(r['id'],r['title']);h=r['hypothesis'];print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r11s2 Decode-preselected local feedback for bimodal predictor training\nPreserve the 64-entry folded-PC bimodal predictor's exact decisions,\nupdate timing and EX correction schedule. Replace its variable-index\nread-modify-write training path with 64 fixed local saturating-counter\nfeedback loops, selected by a one-hot row mask registered alongside\nthe existing ID/EX instruction. This is one predictor training topology\nchange. No additional pipeline, recovery or training cycle is added.\n\nIn ID form index = in.pc[7:2] XOR in.pc[13:8]. At the ordinary ID/EX\npayload capture edge register 64 mask bits, where mask[k] is true only\nfor a decoder-validated legal conditional branch at index k. Reset the\nmask to zero. Hold it whenever ID/EX holds, including load-use, older\ndata-memory and M-unit backpressure. Use the existing payload capture\nenable, independently of recovery and fetch validity: validity-only\nsquash remains authoritative through EX's unchanged train_valid.\nA flush may leave a raw mask on an invalid payload, just as it leaves\nraw instruction fields. No invalid payload can update a counter.\nOn an EX training edge the old mask must refer to that advancing EX\ninstruction, while the newly captured mask refers to its successor.\nKeep this metadata separate from the packed pipeline bundle so its\narchitectural field layout and existing extraction checks remain intact.\n\nPass the mask directly from ID to IF on internal wires. Keep EX's\ntrain_valid, train_taken and train_pc event unchanged. Counter k has\na fixed-address two-bit flop word with update enable\ntrain_valid AND mask[k]; do not read an old counter through train_index\nand then demultiplex a shared computed result. For old state {d,h},\ntaken updates to {d OR h, d OR NOT h}; not-taken updates to\n{d AND h, d AND NOT h}. These implement every two-bit saturating\ntransition, including saturation writes, using only that word's state\nand the qualified outcome. Generate fixed per-word sequential blocks\nso there is no training read mux or late folded-PC wr\n…[10839 of 13911 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:df0be435c42125be]…\nts, decoder default-illegal behavior,\nalignment traps, bounded speculative addresses, redirect-over-imem-stall\npriority, raw payload, held WB operand refresh, load-use/data/M holds,\narithmetic, memory requests and strictly ordered exact-once RVFI.\nKeep all existing correctness assertions and formal progress bounds.\nCheck every counter transition, saturation, capture/hold/reset, training\nqualification, collision ordering, wrong-path stores and M launches.\n\nRequire the unchanged formal/cosim gates and canonical CoreMark CRC,\nUART, bounds and MMIO marker validation. Measure actual marker cycles\nbecause snapshot collisions can change prediction and random-stall phase.\nThe hypothesis targets about six percent fitness improvement primarily\nthrough Fmax; confidence is low until vendor timing and cycle counts\nconfirm it. At the champion's 4378154 cycles, acceptance requires median\nGowin Fmax above 83.683 MHz and fitness above 191.13558 iter/sec.\nAccuracy loss and unchanged ALU/divider paths are the principal risks.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
