{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_30", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261001-002-r10s1','hyp-20261001-002-r12s1','hyp-20261001-003-r10s2']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title']);h=d['hypothesis'];print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h); print('error',str(d.get('error'))[:3500]);print('notes',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-002-r10s1 Four-entry shift-register fetch queue with fall-through decode\nDecouple physical fetch from decode using exactly four flop-based\nshift-register slots, three-bit occupancy 0..4, and empty-queue\nfall-through. This is one structural frontend-buffering change.\nPreserve the execution pipeline, arithmetic units and predictor.\n\nSlots contain the existing 66-bit if_id_t layout: full PC, raw\ninstruction, accepted prediction and validity. Declare storage as\nexplicit logic [65:0] slot vectors or separate named packed registers,\nnot an unpacked array of a struct typedef: isolated formal testing\nfound that Yosys misinterprets the typedef-array declaration as one\npayload, while Verilator/Gowin interpret it as four. Explicit vector\nstorage must pass the unmodified checks; never work around this by\naltering the formal configuration. Keep a separate physical fetch PC driving\nio_imemAddr. Present fixed queue[0] when nonempty, otherwise the\nincoming physical PC/instruction/prediction. Expose head_available\nindependently of flush as occupancy!=0 OR io_imemReady; head valid\nadditionally requires no reset, flush or EX recovery. This prevents\navailability from feeding itself through hazard-driven flush logic.\n\nPhysical acceptance is io_imemReady AND occupancy<4, qualified by\nno reset/recovery. Head consumption requires head_available and\nno downstream hold. An incoming instruction consumed through empty\nfall-through advances fetch without entering storage. Otherwise an\naccepted fetch appends at occupancy minus any simultaneous queued\npop. A queued pop shifts slots 1..3 toward fixed slot zero; a\nsimultaneous append overrides the vacated tail. Occupancy changes\nby stored_push minus queued_pop. Distinguish fall-through consumption\nfrom storage dequeue. Use compile-time fixed slot assignments with\ndecoded append enables; do not infer variable-index storage, RAM\nor a circular head mux. When full, decline physical fetch for that\nedge even if a queued head pops, keeping fetch admission dependent\non registered occupancy \n…[19040 of 22112 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f9583aaa04b393df]…\n.\nWrong-path entries must never retire, train, issue memory or launch M.\nPreserve real/ALTOPS arithmetic and the unchanged ten-clock formal\nliveness bounds; empty bypass and immediate corrected fetch acceptance\nadd no ready-bus recovery stage.\n\nRequire independent FIFO token conservation, effective-PC transitions\nand delayed-training references. Cover empty/full, pointer wraparound,\nall push/pop combinations, stable blocked heads, buffered issue during\nimem stalls, long data/M holds, recovery of a full queue, blocked\ncorrected fetches, both branch correction directions, forwarded JALR\nand reset. Adapt old physical-fetch-equals-decode assumptions without\nweakening architectural assertions. Require the unchanged formal,\ncosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds and median vendor timing\ngates. Divider recurrence and the queued-head-to-RF path now limit the\nprototype, so acceptance comes from hiding fetch stalls at approximately\nunchanged Fmax, not from claiming a large clock-rate improvement.\n\nerror None\nnotes \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
