{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_30", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r5s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261001-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Compact tagged last-target prediction for JALR\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion already predicts direct JAL and conditional branches using\n  a 64-entry folded-PC bimodal table. Prior experiments found negligible\n  benefit from enlarging that table, and carrying direct successors into\n  EX did not improve fitness. JALR is still always predicted sequentially,\n  so every indirect call, return and indirect tail transfer pays an EX\n  recovery bubble. A compact target predictor addresses this remaining\n  control-flow loss while retaining the successful direct predictor and\n  validity-only recovery policy.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one small tagged last-target predictor for legal JALR instructions.\n  Start with 16 direct-mapped entries indexed by fetch PC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6].\n  Each entry contains valid, the complete in-range source-PC tag PC[19:2],\n  and the last resolved aligned target PC[19:2]. Require source PC[31:20]\n  to be zero when looking up or allocating. Reset validity only. A lookup\n  is usable only for raw opcode 0x67 with funct3=0 and an exact tag match;\n  reconstruct the stored target as {12'b0, target_word, 2'b00}. On a miss,\n  predict sequentially. Keep the existing BHT/direct-JAL path unchanged.\n\n  Train once when a valid legal non-trapping JALR advances from EX, with\n  the existing !reset, !stall and !m_busy qualifications. Capture its\n  actual forwarded rs1+immediate target after clearing bit zero. Allocate\n  only aligned targets within [0x00000000,0x00100000); invalidate a matching\n  entry if its newly resolved target is unsuitable for speculation.\n  Training must never truncate the architectural target or suppress an\n  architectural redirect. Simultaneous training and lookup see the old\n  table entry; no combinational EX-to-IF target bypass is permitted.\n\n  Distinguish accepted indirect predictions from direct predicted_taken.\n  Carry an indirect-hit bit and the compact predicted target through\n  IF/ID and ID/EX, captured and held with exactly the same payl\n…[3152 of 6224 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:db8c3365aac62cea]…\nce training and existing M-unit ownership. Export\n      qualified JALR training PC, actual target and allocation suitability.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire qualified EX indirect-target training to IF without altering\n      any external ports, hazard policy or nret=1 retirement contract.\n  - file: test/test_if_predictor.py\n    description: |\n      Retain BHT/JAL assertions and add tagged JALR hit/miss, reset,\n      replacement, same-edge old-entry lookup, illegal encoding,\n      bounds/alignment and stalled-fetch metadata checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add dynamic indirect-call/return programs with target changes and\n      table aliases under independent bus stalls. Check correct links,\n      both miss and wrong-target recovery, imem-stall recovery priority,\n      traps, exact PC/order continuity and suppressed wrong-path stores\n      and M operations. Demonstrate removed steady-state JALR bubbles\n      while preserving every existing pipeline assertion.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
