{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*trace*' -g '*profil*' -g '*coremark*' -g '*.elf' -g '*.bin' -g '*.dis*'; cat cores/bench/core.yaml; cat cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv; rg -n 'trace|iss|coremark|bench-' Makefile test/cosim tools/eval tools/agents/hypothesis.py\"", "aggregated_output": "bench/programs/gen_random_trace.py\nbench/programs/coremark/coremark.h\nbench/programs/coremark/coremark.md5\nbench/programs/coremark/docs/coremark_profile_o0_joined.png\nbench/programs/coremark/docs/html/files/coremark-h.html\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 59.061\n  lut4: 4091\n  ff: 1147\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261001-002-r5s1\n  updated: '2026-10-01T04:15:42.103540Z'\n// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\n// (pc + instr + valid) is *combinational* — there is no separate IF/ID\n// flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\n// captures everything one cycle later.\n//\n// Raw instruction predecode and a folded-PC bimodal table predict direct\n// transfers. Squashes affect validity alone, keeping recovery out of the\n// decoder, regfile addresses and ID/EX payload capture.\n//\n// Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n//                 EX-stage redirect).\nmodule if_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  logic              reset,\n  input  logic              stall,            // hold PC (load-use)\n  input  logic              flush,            // invalidate fetch this cycle\n  input  logic              redirect,         // advancing EX misprediction\n  input  logic [31:0]       redirect_target,\n  input  logic              train_valid,\n  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  input  logic [31:0]       train_pc,\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  input  logic              train_taken,\n  output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0]  \n…[15348 of 18420 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9d01243c9fce86be]…\n.py:148:    # Split ELFs into full-trace cosim vs CRC-validated coremark.\ntools/eval/cosim.py:150:    trace_elfs = [p for p in all_elfs if p.name != \"coremark.elf\"]\ntools/eval/cosim.py:151:    coremark   = next((p for p in all_elfs if p.name == \"coremark.elf\"), None)\ntools/eval/cosim.py:153:    if not trace_elfs and coremark is None:\ntools/eval/cosim.py:156:    # 1. Full-trace cosim of small ELFs (parallel).\ntools/eval/cosim.py:159:                   for elf in trace_elfs for flags in TRACE_STALL_MODES}\ntools/eval/cosim.py:170:    if coremark is not None:\ntools/eval/cosim.py:171:        cm_result = run_coremark_crc(coremark, sim_bin, worktree, env)\ntools/eval/cosim.py:179:    tested = len(trace_elfs) + (1 if coremark else 0)\ntools/eval/test_formal_reclassify.py:86:def test_only_genchecks_traceback_no_sby_output():\ntools/eval/test_remove_path.py:19:    remove_path(tmp_path / \"missing\")                # absent is fine\ntools/eval/rvfi_lint.py:11:exact mirror image of the legitimate single-issue tie of channel 1\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n x=json.loads(l)\n if x.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print('\\\\nID', x['id'],x['title'])\n  print('Fitness/Fmax/cycles:', x.get('fitness'),x.get('fmax_mhz'),x.get('cycles'))\n  if x['id'].endswith(('r3s2','r4s2')):\n   h=x['hypothesis']\n   print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n   print('Notes:',x.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n x=json.loads(l)\n if x.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print('\\\\nID', x['id'],x['title'])\n  print('Fitness/Fmax/cycles:', x.get('fitness'),x.get('fmax_mhz'),x.get('cycles'))\n  if x['id'].endswith(('r3s2','r4s2')):\n   h=x['hypothesis']\n   print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n   print('Notes:',x.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 64-entry folded-PC bimodal prediction at fetch\nFitness/Fmax/cycles: 13.51 5.66 4190307\n\nID hyp-20261001-003-r2s2 Compact bimodal direct-transfer prediction on the registered-divider champion\nFitness/Fmax/cycles: 75.79 31.759 4190281\n\nID hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 Compact bimodal prediction with validity-only recovery\nFitness/Fmax/cycles: 112.68 47.218 4190281\nAdd one compact direct-control-flow predictor to the current five-step\ndivider core: 64 two-bit saturating counters indexed by PC[7:2] XOR\nPC[13:8], initialized to weakly not taken (01), and direct JAL\nprediction. Keep the existing divider lifecycle, arithmetic, register\nforwarding and pipeline depth. The distinguishing implementation is\nvalidity-only recovery: a misprediction kills the younger instruction\nby clearing its ID/EX valid bit, without masking its instruction word\nor using recovery to clear every ID/EX payload register. This removes\nthe late EX-to-IF-to-regfile-address and EX-to-wide-ID-payload recovery\ncones while retaining the measured small predictor's cycle benefit.\n\nPredecode raw imem_data independently of any squash signal. Predict\nconditional branches only for opcode 0x63 with funct3 in {0,1,4,5,6,7};\npredict opcode 0x6f JAL taken unconditionally. Compute the B/J target\nfrom the fetch PC and immediate. Select it only when word aligned\nand within [0x00000000,0x00100000); otherwise select PC+4. JALR stays\nsequential. Lookup uses the old counter value on simultaneous training,\nwith no EX-to-IF training bypass. Install the selected PC only on an\naccepted fetch; architectural recovery overrides frontend stalls.\n\nCarry only an effective predicted_taken bit in IF/ID and ID/EX, using\nthe same instruction acceptance and hold controls. This bit records\nwhether the direct target actually passed alignment/bounds gating and\nwas selected. Branch/JAL direct targets are determined by the accepted\nPC and instruction, so no 32-bit predicted-next-PC register or EX target\nequality comparator is required. A valid, advancing ordinary EX\ninst\n…[4875 of 7947 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a90f87f4943f3bdb]…\nistory\npredictor. The accepted instruction fixes its B/J target, so the\nexisting one-bit direction check remains sufficient.\n\nThis is one predictor target-datapath change: move already-required\nsuccessor arithmetic to the fetch acceptance boundary and remove its\nredundant EX copies. Preserve EX resolution timing, redirect priority\nover frontend stalls, wrong-path suppression, all forwarding and\ndivider behavior, and the ten-clock ready-bus liveness limit. Retain\nthe nret=1 port contract, decoder trap discipline and every eval gate.\n\nRequire unchanged CoreMark marker cycles and canonical CRC/UART output,\ncosim and formal correctness, and score the vendor median Fmax rather\nthan predicting a cycle gain. A six percent frequency improvement\nwould lift fitness from 112.68 to about 119.44; this is an unmeasured\ntiming hypothesis, and the reported ALU critical path may limit it.\n\nNotes: \n\nID hyp-20261001-003-r5s2 LUT-RAM bimodal predictor with serialized cold initialization\nFitness/Fmax/cycles: 121.01 52.98 4378154\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The existing BHT already removes most branch bubbles. Prior attempts to carry target PCs into EX and move the counters into LUT RAM did not improve fitness. I’m focusing on the BHT’s update circuit: local counter feedback could remove the shared training read mux and reduce routing cost, though any gain will depend on FPGA timing."}}
