al_ns': 28.038, 'logic_cells': 17, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}}\nThe champion already has a 64-entry folded-PC bimodal predictor and\ndirect JAL prediction. Earlier modeling found negligible benefit from\nincreasing its direction-table capacity, so another direction-only\nchange is unlikely to clear the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold.\nFetch already computes the direct target and sequential successor,\nbut EX recomputes PC-relative targets and PC+4 while verifying the\naccepted prediction. Reusing registered successors can reduce target\narithmetic, mux depth and routing in the \n…[6891 of 9963 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6c22cd31a69129a6]…\nred exact-once RVFI retirement unchanged. Test all\neight counter transitions, independent fetch/train addresses, aliases,\nsame-edge old-value reads, saturation writes, interrupted reset sweeps\nand training attempts during initialization. Exercise direct JAL and\nbranch recovery throughout warmup under independent bus stalls. Require\nunchanged correctness gates and canonical CRC/UART/MMIO bounds; accept\nonly measured vendor median Fmax times actual iterations/cycle above\n130.52 iterations/second. Check that synthesis really reduces counter\nregisters and maps the array into LUT RAM; an unchanged netlist is not\nevidence for this hypothesis.\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r6s2 Locally updated banked flop BHT without a training read mux\n{'fitness': 136.61, 'delta_pct': 1.27, 'cycles': 4378154, 'fmax_mhz': 59.809, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_addr_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -12.976, 'arrival_ns': 23.27, 'logic_cells': 23, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The prior attempts leave little room for prediction accuracy gains: even eliminating every remaining branch error and JALR redirect would save only about 1.3% of cycles. The champion’s worst path now reaches the fetch PC through EX, so I’m focusing on registering misprediction recovery to shorten that path, at the cost of one extra cycle per correction."}}
